k/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tejasprasad2008-afk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tejasprasad2008-afk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tejasprasad2008-afk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tejasprasad2008-afk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tejasprasad2008-afk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tejasprasad2008-afk/TraceTree/commits/38915b19ecc263cb33aa74257117066ea19b9769/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-30T15:10:58Z","email":"tejasprasad2008@gmail.com","name":"Tejas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-30T15:10:58Z","email":"tejasprasad2008@gmail.com","name":"Tejas"},"message":"fix: reduce false positives and make RF model auto-train on first run\n\n- parser.py: add uname/lsb_release to BENIGN_BINARIES (was only in signatures.py); lower mprotect PROT_EXEC severity 9.0→3.0 (shared lib loading triggered critical override every pip install)\n- timeline.py: filter benign execve from burst_process_spawn; raise rapid_file_enumeration threshold 10→50 (pip reads 300+ files normally)\n- detector.py: auto-train RandomForest from local CSV on first run instead of silently falling back to IsolationForest; remove GCS fetch from analyze path (offline-safe)\n- trainer.py: read existing ingested_training_data.csv first to skip redundant sandbox re-runs\n- ingest_malwarebazaar.py: add missing temporal_pattern_count column to CSV output (9→10 features)\n- cli.py: clarify training UI text\n- sandbox/Dockerfile: split wine64 into optional RUN so ARM64 builds succeed\n- sandbox/sandbox.py: retry build with nocache=True on stale cache; fix shell injection — pass log path via env var and execute via tempfile instead of shell -c\n- monitor/scanner.py: add # noscan / # nosec inline suppression support for intentional false positives\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonne