sprasad2008-afk/TraceTree/commits/092204908248a580f93a45561c259a018da325ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-18T11:30:44Z","email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-18T11:30:44Z","email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"},"message":"🔒 [security] Remove hardcoded API keys in production fallback\n\n🎯 **What:** Removed hardcoded API keys from `api/main.py` and enforced mandatory configuration via the `TRACETREE_API_KEYS` environment variable.\n\n⚠️ **Risk:** Hardcoded keys in the codebase pose a significant security risk, as they can be easily discovered by unauthorized parties or accidentally leaked. The previous fallback mechanism allowed the API to start in a vulnerable state if the environment variable was missing.\n\n🛡️ **Solution:**\n- Eliminated hardcoded fallback strings in `os.getenv`.\n- Implemented a startup check that raises a `RuntimeError` if `TRACETREE_API_KEYS` is not set or is empty.\n- Added robust parsing to strip whitespace and filter empty keys from the environment variable.\n- Added a new test suite `tests/test_api_security.py` to verify the authentication logic and configuration enforcement.\n\nCo-authored-by: tejasprasad2008-afk <242620744+tejasprasad2008-afk@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c4b469b310516c8c429c5d107dcc33a155769921","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tejasprasad2008-afk/TraceTree/git/trees/c4b469b310516c8c429c5d107dcc33a155769921"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tejasprasad2008-afk/TraceTree/git/commits/092204908248a580f93a45561c259a018da325ff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/842251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api