hub.com/users/falese/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/780f8f0e077467abccb8c44ca5cbcf93cd21b670/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:07:56Z","email":"falese@gmail.com","name":"Sean Falese"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T17:07:56Z","email":"falese@gmail.com","name":"Sean Falese"},"message":"fix(mlx): pass --extra-eos-token so generation halts at the model''s end token\n\nQuantized chat models are routinely packaged with `config.json`''s\n`eos_token_id` disagreeing with `tokenizer_config.json`''s `eos_token`.\nQwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct-4bit ships 151643 (`<|endoftext|>`) as the former\nand `<|im_end|>` (151645) as the latter. The chat-tuned model ends its turn\nwith the token the *tokenizer* names, which is not in the stop set, so\ngeneration never halts: it runs to `--max-tokens` and pads the tail with\nfiller (`!<|im_end|>` repeated to the cap).\n\n`resolveExtraEosTokens` reads the model''s `added_tokens.json` and names the\nchat end tokens it actually contains. The intersection is required: mlx_lm\nraises `ValueError: ''<token>'' is not a token for this tokenizer` for anything\nit does not know, so passing a fixed list breaks every model that lacks one.\nA model given as a bare repo id has no local directory to read and degrades\nto passing nothing.\n\nMeasured on the intent-manifest adaptor, same prompt, byte-identical output:\n\n  before   400 tokens (hits the cap)   ~25 s\n  after    140-149 tokens              ~9-11 s\n\nThis also fixes the streaming path, which `stripChatEndToken` could not\nprotect: the special token is filtered out of the SSE stream, so consumers\nreceived the filler with no marker to truncate on. A `coder serve` stream now\nends exactly at the manifest — `{\"type\":\"done\",\"totalTokens\":140}`, zero\ntrailing filler — which is what the plugin-coder `serve` transport needs.\n\n506 tests pass, tsc --noEmit clean, eslint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RFeTqY6wwR1q1dDUQUgEwT","tree":{"sha":"1e6688f7ed453aa23bbbce583f31ab5215181f0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/git/trees/1e6688f7ed453aa23bbbce583f31ab5215181f0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/git/commits/780f8f0e077467abccb8c44ca5cbcf93cd21b670","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9287957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/falese","id":9287957,"login":"falese","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODc5NTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/coder/commit/780f8f0e077467abccb8c44ca5cbcf93cd21b670","node_id":"C_kwDORtCmEtoAKDc4MGY4ZjBlMDc3NDY3YWJjY2I4YzQ0Y2E1Y2JjZjkzY2QyMWI2NzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/coder/commit/5fb4026c94b6a12c935f10d86748b93088075bf8","sha":"5fb4026c94b6a12c935f10d86748b93088075bf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/5fb4026c94b6a12c935f10d86748b93088075bf8"}],"sha"