url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/coder/commit/5fb4026c94b6a12c935f10d86748b93088075bf8","node_id":"C_kwDORtCmEtoAKDVmYjQwMjZjOTRiNmExMmM5MzVmMTBkODY3NDhiOTMwODgwNzViZjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/coder/commit/52eff673722926ade55e538501bbfb653ab05b08","sha":"52eff673722926ade55e538501bbfb653ab05b08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/52eff673722926ade55e538501bbfb653ab05b08"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/coder/commit/071af853b1242a7034b6662b2e6d20e3b8a2933d","sha":"071af853b1242a7034b6662b2e6d20e3b8a2933d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/071af853b1242a7034b6662b2e6d20e3b8a2933d"}],"sha":"5fb4026c94b6a12c935f10d86748b93088075bf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/5fb4026c94b6a12c935f10d86748b93088075bf8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9287957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/falese","id":9287957,"login":"falese","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODc5NTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/071af853b1242a7034b6662b2e6d20e3b8a2933d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:08:16Z","email":"falese@gmail.com","name":"Sean Falese"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:08:16Z","email":"falese@gmail.com","name":"Sean Falese"},"message":"feat(intent-manifest): train, eval and verify the intent→manifest adaptor (M3-M6)\n\nCompletes the milestones from falese/seans-mfe-tool#364 that need an MLX\nruntime, and fixes the harness defects the first real run exposed.\n\nResults (Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct-4bit + LoRA r=8, 200 iters, 39 min,\n7.18 GB peak, val loss 2.112 → 0.047, adapter 44 MB):\n\n  run                          weights  system prompt   pass-rate\n  baseline, original prompt    —        buggy grammar   0.848 (28/33)\n  baseline, corrected prompt   —        corrected       1.000 (33/33)\n  tuned                        LoRA     corrected       1.000 (33/33)\n  ablation, base               —        none            0.000 (0/33)\n  ablation, tuned              LoRA     none            0.939 (31/33)\n\nM5''s `lift >= +0.15` gate reads +0.000 and is unreachable as specified. The\nopening 0.848 was measuring a defect in this pack''s own prompts/system.md —\nprovidesSlots documented as slot-id strings where the DSL requires\n[{id, description?}] — and all five failures were that one line. With the\ngrammar corrected the base model clears the held-out set from the prompt\nalone, so the ceiling is 1.000. The set shares a generator with the training\npairs and cannot separate the models. The measurable axis is the ablation:\nstrip the 1,172-token grammar prompt and the base model scores 0/33 (it\nwrites prose advice) while the tuned model scores 31/33. Gate M5 there.\n\nM6 end-to-end: a held-out intent produced a manifest that passed\nparseAndValidateDirectory (valid, 0 errors), drove remote:generate (23 files,\n0 skipped) and passed all 7 mfe:validate gates with no hand edit to the DSL.\n\nHarness fixes, each with tests:\n\n- eval: new optional per-pack evals/eval.config.json (src/eval/pack-config.ts)\n  — dimension weights (renormalised; a zero-weight dimension is skipped, not\n  scored 0, and prints n/a), artifact extension/prompt-prepend, eval-time\n  system prompt applied to baseline runs too, and a token cap. Absent file =\n  historic behaviour, so react-ts is untouched. This pack weights tests alone,\n  so its composite IS the DSL validator pass-rate.\n- eval: runEval wrote `prompt + \"\\n\" + generated` into the scored artifact.\n  Correct for a code pack whose prompt is import context; for a prose prompt\n  it handed the validator English followed by YAML, which could never pass.\n- mlx: --system-prompt takes the prompt TEXT, not a path. Every\n  `coder generate --system <file>` was giving the model the literal path\n  string as its system message. systemFile is now read at the boundary;\n  systemPrompt carries literal text (serve).\n- mlx: stripChatEndToken truncates at the first chat end token. A model that\n  does not halt on EOS fills the token cap with filler — `coder generate`\n  was emitting valid YAML followed by 120 lines of `!<|im_end|>`, which would\n  have reached plugin-coder''s compileIntent intact.\n- pack: eval_suite.ts asserts on the formatted validator errors, so a failing\n  record names the rule it broke. This is how the providesSlots bug surfaced.\n\n500 tests pass, tsc --noEmit clean, eslint clean.\n\nRefs falese/seans-mfe-tool#364\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RFeTqY6wwR1q1dDUQUgEwT","tree":{"sha":"791f8eca8da1577600a0c2a0fdc836cf45cfeb6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/git/trees/791f8eca8da1577600a0c2a0fdc836cf45cfeb6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/git/commits/071af853b1242a7034b6662b2e6d20e3b8a2933d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9287957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/falese","id":9287957,"login":"falese","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODc5NTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/coder/commit/071af853b1242a7034b6662b2e6d20e3b8a2933d","node_id":"C_kwDORtCmEtoAKDA3MWFmODUzYjEyNDJhNzAzNGI2NjYyYjJlNmQyMGUzYjhhMjkzM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/coder/commit/df963fc98f756acfcbae3444af3bc8feca497166","sha":"df963fc98f756acfcbae3444af3bc8feca497166","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/df963fc98f756acfcbae3444af3bc8feca497166"}],"sha":"071af853b1242a7034b6662b2e6d20e3b8a2933d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/071af853b1242a7034b6662b2e6d20e3b8a2933d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/df963fc98f756acfcbae3444af3bc8feca497166/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T02:59:39Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T02:59:39Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(adaptors): scaffold intent-manifest adaptor (M0-M2)\n\nAdd the intent→manifest adaptor pack: compiles a business intent into a\nschema-valid seans-mfe mfe-manifest.yaml. This is the platform side''s\ngenerative lane (seans-mfe-tool PDR-009/ADR-084/ADR-085), tracked as\nfalese/seans-mfe-tool#364. Covers the milestones that need no MLX runtime:\n\n- M0 Scaffold: manifest.json (ManifestSchema-valid), train-config.toml\n  (TrainConfigSchema-valid, portable relative paths), no-op extract.json,\n  evals/eval_suite.ts, README, .gitignore. Mirrors the react-ts pack shape.\n- M1 Data: install the 660-pair corpus (canonical copy in\n  seans-mfe-tool/docs/corpus/intent-manifest; train/valid git-ignored,\n  eval.jsonl committed). Verified with coder''s own tooling —\n  `data validate` 564/564 valid; `data stats` 660 pairs, prompt mean 33,\n  completion mean 209, dup 0% (inside the >=500 / <200 / <400 / <5% bar).\n  All 660 completions pass the DSL validateFull oracle.\n- M2 System prompt: prompts/system.md encodes the DSL grammar — required\n  fields, type/language enums, the capability array-of-single-key-map shape,\n  the before/main/after/error lifecycle, \"emit only YAML\" — with two\n  in-context examples (a minimal remote and a data-BFF) drawn from the corpus.\n\nEval oracle: evals/eval_suite.ts uses `validateManifestText` from the\nfirst-party @seans-mfe/plugin-coder (ADR-088); adaptors/** is excluded from\ncoder''s tsc/eslint, so it never touches coder''s gates. That package must be\nlink-resolvable from the eval sandbox (documented in the pack README).\n\nRemaining (need a coder + mlx_lm session, ~18GB Apple Silicon): M3 baseline,\nM4 train, M5 eval + lift gate, M6 end-to-end.\n\nRefs falese/seans-mfe-tool#364\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P7vBUpiNVSxAUjUruDoWjh","tree":{"sha":"7b6e2684742fe8e23800a8535f693714eabf52da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/git/trees/7b6e2684742fe8e23800a8535f693714eabf52da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/git/commits/df963fc98f756acfcbae3444af3bc8feca497166","verification":{"payload":"tree 7b6e2684742fe8e23800a8535f693714eabf52da\nparent 52eff673722926ade55e538501bbfb653ab05b08\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788231579 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788231579 +0000\n\nfeat(adaptors): scaffold intent-manifest adaptor (M0-M2)\n\nAdd the intent→manifest adaptor pack: compiles a business intent into a\nschema-valid seans-mfe mfe-manifest.yaml. This is the platform side''s\ngenerative lane (seans-mfe-tool PDR-009/ADR-084/ADR-085), tracked as\nfalese/seans-mfe-tool#364. Covers the milestones that need no MLX runtime:\n\n- M0 Scaffold: manifest.json (ManifestSchema-valid), train-config.toml\n  (TrainConfigSchema-valid, portable relative paths), no-op extract.json,\n  evals/eval_suite.ts, README, .gitignore. Mirrors the react-ts pack shape.\n- M1 Data: install the 660-pair corpus (canonical copy in\n  seans-mfe-tool/docs/corpus/intent-manifest; train/valid git-ignored,\n  eval.jsonl committed). Verified with coder''s own tooling —\n  `data validate` 564/564 valid; `data stats` 660 pairs, prompt mean 33,\n  completion mean 209, dup 0% (inside the >=500 / <200 / <400 / <5% bar).\n  All 660 completions pass the DSL validateFull oracle.\n- M2 System prompt: prompts/system.md encodes the DSL grammar — required\n  fields, type/language enums, the capability array-of-single-key-map shape,\n  the before/main/after/error lifecycle, \"emit only YAML\" — with two\n  in-context examples (a minimal remote and a data-BFF) drawn from the corpus.\n\nEval oracle: evals/eval_suite.ts uses `validateManifestText` from the\nfirst-party @seans-mfe/plugin-coder (ADR-088); adaptors/** is excluded from\ncoder''s tsc/eslint, so it never touches coder''s gates. That package must be\nlink-resolvable from the eval sandbox (documented in the pack README).\n\nRemaining (need a coder + mlx_lm session, ~18GB Apple Silicon): M3 baseline,\nM4 train, M5 eval + lift gate, M6 end-to-end.\n\nRefs falese/seans-mfe-tool#364\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P7vBUpiNVSxAUjUruDoWjh\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDtJw9A8\n2JZa0QZRaio47Ml40BgXW5JBJzdElJ3UTeVZk4l2ZssJ4DXsaZBbs+o9UczoQ0vK40CiCXRpO9gm\nEgs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T02:59:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"htt