s (first real gate run — the web sandbox can''t\nbun install):\n\n- loadConfig''s existing-file branch expanded adaptors/models/logs dirs but not\n  episodes_dir/graph_dir, so a config.toml that already exists kept literal\n  ~/.coder paths (recorder/graph would write to a bogus relative dir). The\n  missing-file branch already expanded them; add the two lines to the\n  existing-file branch. Fixes config-loader \"expand ~ from the config file\".\n\n- The /generate messages[] dry-run test asserted the SSE body contains\n  <|im_start|>, but parseChannels intentionally strips <|…|> tokens and the\n  holdback splits tokens. Assert on the prior-turn content folded into the\n  prompt instead; the ChatML shape is already covered by buildPromptFromBody.\n\nRefs #60\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01YXSXnrQYgLtvccTgpsutiu","tree":{"sha":"92af644d69f060c168e41f2ed604e8dc22a6b352","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/git/trees/92af644d69f060c168e41f2ed604e8dc22a6b352"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/git/commits/a150ac3e24f201de5fc06eb60d2ef8477a7bc4e4","verification":{"payload":"tree 92af644d69f060c168e41f2ed604e8dc22a6b352\nparent c829b5e336970c5dc7651715847bbab00a9ff576\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1781184410 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1781184410 +0000\n\nfix: expand episodes_dir/graph_dir when loading an existing config; fix serve test\n\nCI on PR #61 surfaced two failures (first real gate run — the web sandbox can''t\nbun install):\n\n- loadConfig''s existing-file branch expanded adaptors/models/logs dirs but not\n  episodes_dir/graph_dir, so a config.toml that already exists kept literal\n  ~/.coder paths (recorder/graph would write to a bogus relative dir). The\n  missing-file branch already expanded them; add the two lines to the\n  existing-file branch. Fixes config-loader \"expand ~ from the config file\".\n\n- The /generate messages[] dry-run test asserted the SSE body contains\n  <|im_start|>, but parseChannels intentionally strips <|…|> tokens and the\n  holdback splits tokens. Assert on the prior-turn content folded into the\n  prompt instead; the ChatML shape is already covered by buildPromptFromBody.\n\nRefs #60\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01YXSXnrQYgLtvccTgpsutiu\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNf7jEPb\nzUC5tH8AEtSUt7woWt3Z+DXsgSckrH0eu6u/kRt0MtWRocqVSPGWjD1pj/3kCBRaI4WUWh4pkv5f\nkgM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-11T13:26:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/coder/commit/a150ac3e24f201de5fc06eb60d2ef8477a7bc4e4","node_id":"C_kwDORtCmEtoAKGExNTBhYzNlMjRmMjAxZGU1ZmMwNmViNjBkMmVmODQ3N2E3YmM0ZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/coder/commit/c829b5e336970c5dc7651715847bbab00a9ff576","sha":"c829b5e336970c5dc7651715847bbab00a9ff576","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/c829b5e336970c5dc7651715847bbab00a9ff576"}],"sha":"a150ac3e24f201de5fc06eb60d2ef8477a7bc4e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/a150ac3e24f201de5fc06eb60d2ef8477a7bc4e4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/c829b5e336970c5dc7651715847bbab00a9ff576/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T20:36:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T20:36:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat: persona/voice LoRA via the SSD engine with a pluggable thread-recall verifier\n\nClose the self-learning loop: turn captured episodes into a persona/voice LoRA\nand prove it learned — reusing the proven SSD recipe (self-sample → verifier-\nfilter → train winners → commit-if-improves / rollback) rather than a parallel\nSFT path. The engine is unchanged; only the verifier is swapped.\n\nPluggable verifier:\n- sampler.sampleCompletions gains an optional verifier {scoreSample, prepareCompletion};\n  when set it scores samples with it (e.g. thread-recall) and skips the code\n  scorers. Default path (tsc/eslint/tests) is byte-identical.\n- self-improve gains one optional dep `loadPool` to override the sampling pool.\n  All gate/rollback/divergence logic is reused as-is.\n\nPersona verifier/eval (src/eval/persona.ts):\n- threadRecall (precision/recall/F1, normalized, no embeddings — honors spec),\n  scoreThreadRecall (per-sample), runPersonaEval (over persona-eval.jsonl, dry-run\n  stub), toEvalSummary adapter, loadPersonaPool, formatPersonaTable.\n\nEpisodes -> persona pack:\n- episodeToPersonaRecords (voice-only completion + reference threads).\n- src/adaptors/scaffold.ts + `coder adaptor scaffold <name> --from-episodes`:\n  builds a schema-valid pack (manifest + train-config.toml) and data/train.jsonl\n  (voice seed) + persona-pool.jsonl (in-loop refs) + persona-eval.jsonl (held-out).\n\nWiring (coder adaptor):\n- `self-improve --persona` runs the SSD engine with the thread-recall verifier\n  (pool/scorer/eval from the pack); `eval --persona` scores + writes persona_f1.\n- Manifest gains optional persona_f1; observability gains persona_eval_complete.\n\nVoice stays in the LoRA; knowledge/threads stay in the graph (modular). Closes:\nthink -> episode -> graph -> scaffold -> train -> eval -> serve --adaptor -> think.\n\nTests: persona (threadRecall/runPersonaEval/scoreThreadRecall), scaffold (valid\npack + deterministic split + dedupe), sampler verifier path, self-improve loadPool,\nepisodeToPersonaRecords, and a dry-run E2E integration. Docs: spec + CLAUDE.md.\n\nNote: gates (tsc/eslint/bun test) could not run in the web sandbox (npm registry\nblocked, no bun install); transpile-checked + contract-verified manually. CI must\nconfirm.\n\nRefs #60\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01YXSXnrQYgLtvccTgpsutiu","tree":{"sha":"03f2e1daf9cc1725f527489468ec7c82f57780c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/git/trees/03f2e1daf9cc1725f527489468ec7c82f57780c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/git/commits/c829b5e336970c5dc7651715847bbab00a9ff576","verification":{"payload":"tree 03f2e1daf9cc1725f527489468ec7c82f57780c5\nparent 0ccbaa5b496dfdd85d251eb89408dda6a6f2c450\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780864589 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780864589 +0000\n\nfeat: persona/voice LoRA via the SSD engine with a pluggable thread-recall verifier\n\nClose the self-learning loop: turn captured episodes into a persona/voice LoRA\nand prove it learned — reusing the proven SSD recipe (self-sample → verifier-\nfilter → train winners → commit-if-improves / rollback) rather than a parallel\nSFT path. The engine is unchanged; only the verifier is swapped.\n\nPluggable verifier:\n- sampler.sampleCompletions gains an optional verifier {scoreSample, prepareCompletion};\n  when set it scores samples with it (e.g. thread-recall) and skips the code\n  scorers. Default path (tsc/eslint/tests) is byte-identical.\n- self-improve gains one optional dep `loadPool` to override the sampling pool.\n  All gate/rollback/divergence logic is reused as-is.\n\nPersona verifier/eval (src/eval/persona.ts):\n- threadRecall (precision/recall/F1, normalized, no embeddings — honors spec),\n  scoreThreadRecall (per-sample), runPersonaEval (over persona-eval.jsonl, dry-run\n  stub), toEvalSummary adapter, loadPersonaPool, formatPersonaTable.\n\nEpisodes -> persona pack:\n- episodeToPersonaRecords (voice-only completion + reference threads).\n- src/adaptors/scaffold.ts + `coder adaptor scaffold <name> --from-episodes`:\n  builds a schema-valid pack (manifest + train-config.toml) and data/train.jsonl\n  (voice seed) + persona-pool.jsonl (in-loop refs) + persona-eval.jsonl (held-out).\n\nWiring (coder adaptor):\n- `self-improve --persona` runs the SSD engine with the thread-recall verifier\n  (pool/scorer/eval from the pack); `eval --persona` scores + writes persona_f1.\n- Manifest gains optional persona_f1; observability gains persona_eval_complete.\n\nVoice stays in the LoRA; knowledge/threads stay in the graph (modular). Closes:\nthink -> episode -> graph -> scaffold -> train -> eval -> serve --adaptor -> think.\n\nTests: persona (threadRecall/runPersonaEval/scoreThreadRecall), scaffold (valid\npack + deterministic split + dedupe), sampler verifier path, self-improve loadPool,\nepisodeToPersonaRecords, and a dry-run E2E integration. Docs: spec + CLAUDE.md.\n\nNote: gates (tsc/eslint/bun test) could not run in the web sandbox (npm registry\nblocked, no bun install); transpile-checked + contract-verified manually. CI must\nconfirm.\n\nRefs #60\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01YXSXnrQYgLtvccTgpsutiu\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIqL8+Zs\nUW/I0i4lInw/LOswgfuR2uehIRTbxS5J0JnQ9353gGN5SiOAaY3ZNyJDN7/K4r7SqNIQXY2Tleqo\nIgg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-07T20:36:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/coder/commit/c829b5e336970c5dc7651715847bbab00a9ff576","node_id":"C_kwDORtCmEtoAKGM4MjliNWUzMzY5NzBjNWRjNzY1MTcxNTg0N2JiYWIwMGE5ZmY1NzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/coder/commit/0ccbaa5b496dfdd85d251eb89408dda6a6f2c450","sha":"0ccbaa5b496dfdd85d251eb89408dda6a6f2c450","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/0ccbaa5b496dfdd85d251eb89408dda6a6f2c450"}],"sha":"c829b5e336970c5dc7651715847bbab00a9ff576","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/c829b5e336970c5dc7651715847bbab00a9ff576"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/commits/0ccbaa5b496dfdd85d251eb89408dda6a6f2c450/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-07T19:46:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-07T19:46:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat: episodes + knowledge graph (cross-turn memory, capture, build/query, JSONL bake)\n\nAdd the rich memory substrate of the self-learning loop on top of the SSD\npipeline: multi-turn episodes captured from coder serve, a knowledge graph\nbuilt from their concept threads, and a bridge that bakes episodes into the\nexisting data/train pipeline.\n\nCross-turn memory:\n- /generate accepts messages[] + sessionId; buildPromptFromBody windows + ChatML-\n  formats prior turns server-side (reuses formatPrompt/applyWindow from\n  chat/history). Single-prompt requests unchanged.\n\nEpisodes (src/episodes/):\n- types/threads/store/recorder: Episode schema (turns w/ thought+final + concept\n  threads), parseThreads/stripThreads, save/load/list, episodeToJsonl bake bridge,\n  and a SessionRecorder that accumulates exchanges by sessionId.\n- serve records each completed exchange; POST /episodes/save flushes a session;\n  serve command runs an idle-timeout fallback sweep + flush-all on shutdown.\n- coder episodes list/show/export.\n\nKnowledge graph (src/graph/):\n- build/store/query: threads -> nodes (episode counts), within-episode\n  co-occurrence -> weighted edges (JSON-keyed pairs, collision-free). Pure builder.\n- coder graph build/show/query. Consumption = bake into training data;\n  inference-time RAG/graph-retrieval stays out of scope (spec unchanged).\n\nConfig: add episodes_dir + graph_dir. Observability: episode_saved + graph_built.\nDocs: spec.md + CLAUDE.md resolved decisions. Tests: episodes/{threads,store,\nrecorder}, graph/{build,query}, serve (messages[]/buildPromptFromBody, episode\nrecording, /episodes/save), config keys.\n\nNote: gates (tsc/eslint/bun test) could not run in the web sandbox (npm registry\nblocked, no bun install); transpile-checked + contract-verified manually. CI must\nconfirm.\n\nRefs #60\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01YXSXnrQYgLtvccTgpsutiu","tree":{"sha":"6bb3122b7a3cfc94921e5f100e38cd9e2f0d4c8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/git/trees/6bb3122b7a3cfc94921e5f100e38cd9e2f0d4c8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/coder/git/commits/0ccbaa5b496dfdd85d251eb89408dda6a6f2c450","verification":{"payload":"tree 6bb3122b7a3cfc94921e5f100e38cd9e2f0d4c8c\nparent db1ae44baba611fca869087c909673e870e452a9\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780861563 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1780861563 +0000\n\nfeat: episodes + knowledge graph (cross-turn memory, capture, build/query, JSONL bake)\n\nAdd the rich memory substrate of the self-learning loop on top of the SSD\npipeline: multi-turn episodes captured from coder serve, a knowledge graph\nbuilt from their concept threads, and a bridge that bakes episodes into the\nexisting data/train pipeline.\n\nCross-turn memory:\n- /generate accepts messages[] + sessionId; buildPromptFromBody windows + ChatML-\n  formats prior turns server-side (reuses formatPrompt/applyWindow from\n  chat/history). Single-prompt requests unchanged.\n\nEpisodes (src/episodes/):\n- types/threads/store/recorder: Episode schema (turns w/ thought+final + concept\n  threads), parseThreads/stripThreads, save/load/list, episodeToJsonl bake bridge,\n  and a SessionRecorder that accumulates exchanges by sessionId.\n- serve records each completed exchange; POST /episodes/save flushes a session;\n  serve command runs an idle-timeout fallback sweep + flush-all on shutdown.\n- coder episodes list/show/export.\n\nKnowledge graph (src/graph/):\n- build/store/query: threads -> nodes (episode counts), within-episode\n  co-occurrence -> weighted edges (JSON-keyed pairs, collision-free). Pure builder.\n- coder graph build/show/query. Consumption = bake into training data;\n  inference-time RAG/graph-retrieval stays out of scope (spec unchanged).\n\nConfig: add episodes_dir + graph_dir. Observability: episode_saved + graph_built.\nDocs: spec.md + CLAUDE.md resolved decisions. Tests: episodes/{threads,store,\nrecorder}, graph/{build,query}, serve (messages[]/buildPromptFromBody, episode\nrecording, /episodes/save), config keys.\n\nNote: gates (tsc/eslint/bun test) could not run in the web sandbox (npm registry\nblocked, no bun install); transpile-checked + contract-verified manually. CI must\nconfirm.\n\nRefs #60\n\nhttps://claude.ai/co