dityaBelhekar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdityaBelhekar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pranavpanchal1326/ARGUS-PRISM/commits/9e461e9740160cf6dcf94f6d2afff194927cfd2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T06:04:13Z","email":"belhekaraditya96@gmail.com","name":"AdityaBelhekar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T06:04:13Z","email":"belhekaraditya96@gmail.com","name":"AdityaBelhekar"},"message":"feat(autostr): sealed evidence packages with zero key material on glass\n\nThe screen that lost V2, rebuilt with the most care (PRD §5.8). Every V2 sin inverted:\n\n- Async job ASSEMBLING → SIGNING → SEALED, generating three packages from real case\n  data: FIU-IND STR (XML), CBI evidence (real reportlab PDF), RBI report (JSON).\n- Downloads stream straight from the DB blob — no filesystem, no memory:// 404.\n  All three verified downloadable (PDF magic bytes checked).\n- Regeneration is a fresh job with fresh timestamps and fresh fingerprints —\n  verifiably different every time (content embeds the generation time).\n- Zero key material crosses the API boundary: responses carry only the 8-char\n  document fingerprint (last 8 of the content SHA-256). The HMAC seal is stored\n  server-side and never serialized — test asserts none of\n  signature/hmac/private/begin/secret/signing_key appear in any response.\n- MLRO countersignature (APPROVE_STR) marks a package SUBMITTED; downloads and\n  approvals are audit-logged.\n\nRuff green; 29/29 tests pass. Contract: 44 paths, 52 schemas.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"27f966c9e32284f4261c61609005bc125113f2a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pranavpanchal1326/ARGUS-PRISM/git/trees/27f966c9e32284f4261c61609005bc125113f2a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pranavpanchal1326/ARGUS-PRISM/git/commits/9e461e9740160cf6dcf94f6d2afff194927cfd2c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsign