om/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/37ca2d604b4d0f59ab7183240a55cbdbd89e5b35/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:48:56Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:48:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: draw the chips beside a question whether she has ever taken a drug apart from the answer (#61)\n\nThe backend''s asksWhetherSheHasTakenADrug key (openmrs-module-chartsearchai ADR Decision 156) is true where the\nquestion asked whether the patient has ever taken one drug. Every chip beside such an answer is now drawn neutral and\ncollapsed behind \"N finding(s) about this patient''s medications\", one click away: they are about that drug''s place in\nher chart, such as \"Metoclopramide interacts with active order Lidocaine — Major\" beside \"Has she ever taken\nMetoclopramide?\", and not a reading of the question. Any other value draws the chips as before.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bd128bfc3aa255cfab44546e1ae3f6e67bb82c1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/bd128bfc3aa255cfab44546e1ae3f6e67bb82c1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/37ca2d604b4d0f59ab7183240a55cbdbd89e5b35","verification":{"payload":"tree bd128bfc3aa255cfab44546e1ae3f6e67bb82c1a\nparent 984a782055ae289f7fc628c7e45d2fadbacd9567\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1791298136 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791298136 +0300\n\nfeat: draw the chips beside a question whether she has ever taken a drug apart from the answer (#61)\n\nThe backend''s asksWhetherSheHasTakenADrug key (openmrs-module-chartsearchai ADR Decision 156) is true where the\nquestion asked whether the patient has ever taken one drug. Every chip beside such an answer is now drawn neutral and\ncollapsed behind \"N finding(s) about this patient''s medications\", one click away: they are about that drug''s place in\nher chart, such as \"Metoclopramide interacts with active order Lidocaine — Major\" beside \"Has she ever taken\nMetoclopramide?\", and not a reading of the question. Any other value draws the chips as before.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQpYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq2YQAE8JXKqps6luCloGPzewb/Fn\nPyH06RxabD29XDQUrXb0owUwk7iLD+HLT0kHAyF+hk23Nf0E/sG9XPejCKQA/zvd\niFQ8lnUW2QuFUZ4ynkwemoS0v+C10IsX0xy75IjArUhIHvgLIe3N2CpEK7uRd+4M\n2sQjP46cud+ftGgwc23O2+71bGiXk6g4bJFiWM3PmkZ3AhmnzTQbhfjm25ji1VzM\nsLXCP7zxIOuuS8iJMzMUTj+qEzhcF/pSB5k+T3AWMCQnAydoOZG0dlD/mU+jRbBe\nwSzGf19iz8hrzsen9gSh/EagIt/YnV5WlfQwo3K6ofjSGXZx5rjLFVVF2C+ox/FG\n2ptGclPHrBj40IgVc7WwJ+JaH5EOUWHWNQAz3m3U9WHxi9GBIu5J9Otd851MkruK\nfCVVjR26FeuK0XdpvRq9g65ATnS3uPCBbvt02ZIIC6E27LHupnSoLC7FeIniXvPb\nL4SF0NJGXF1JNWZlhq65haj4tKm+IAk3cEdqXZaNxaHfxEps65ZHfzqnSCCM9HSm\n2uScc7CDBAQWziPhv1uNdY91bhGrL71SZiXk7aqDRvzem+0jkyoHFfL14VeUVD/k\nMSDapeMokEAyH0O7HEDrnzQW4/MQhUxkquaqvVy5MALxqB7GX7/PPNCmfZJmgeWg\nnijeBvZScMZPCpBcJ5uV\n=LAmJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T14:48:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/37ca2d604b4d0f59ab7183240a55cbdbd89e5b35","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKDM3Y2EyZDYwNGI0ZDBmNTlhYjcxODMyNDBhNTVjYmRiZDg5ZTViMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/984a782055ae289f7fc628c7e45d2fadbacd9567","sha":"984a782055ae289f7fc628c7e45d2fadbacd9567","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/984a782055ae289f7fc628c7e45d2fadbacd9567"}],"sha":"37ca2d604b4d0f59ab7183240a55cbdbd89e5b35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/37ca2d604b4d0f59ab7183240a55cbdbd89e5b35"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/984a782055ae289f7fc628c7e45d2fadbacd9567/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T22:56:11Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T22:56:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: fold each cited chip unless a check names its own finding (#60)\n\n* feat: fold each cited chip unless a check names its own finding\n\nA model answer whose prose checks reported anything drew every chip in full:\non \"…is it safe to give Fluconazole?\" with an ARV list, four long mechanism\nparagraphs under the answer because it stated no severity and paraphrased\none finding. The checks that name findings now keep only those findings''\nchips in full (unfaithful rendering, an unfounded rating, a caution lead\nbeside a withholding finding); an unstated severity keeps none open, the\none-line chip stating the rating the answer left out. The two checks that\nname no finding, and any null measurement, still keep every chip in full.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: fold a chip the module states after the answer, tagged stated above\n\nThe backend now appends, after a model''s answer, the findings about the drug\nproposed against her own orders that the answer left out, in a sentence that\ncites no marker, and names them in findingsStatedByTheModule (backend ADR\nDecision 147). Such a chip is drawn on one line tagged \"Stated above\" rather\nthan in full beside the sentence that just named it. The \"See [n]\" hover no\nlonger says every check found nothing: under the per-chip rule an unstated\nrating may have been reported, which the one line states.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: draw an unmentioned finding against a listed drug on one line\n\nA finding about the drug proposed against a drug the question only lists\n(an interaction naming no order of hers, its subject not one of her\nprescriptions) that the answer does not cite was drawn in full. It rests on\nwhat the question names rather than her orders, so it is now drawn on one\nline tagged \"Not in the answer\", its detail behind Show details, and does not\ncount towards collapsing the box. A finding against one of her own orders\nthe answer leaves out is still drawn in full. notInTheAnswer shares\ncompactChips'' reading of which findings the answer cites.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: draw a reworded cited finding on one line tagged to compare\n\nA cited finding that unfaithfullyRenderedCitations alone names (the answer\nreproduced its record and then said something different inside the same\nsentence) was drawn in full. It is now drawn on one line tagged \"Reworded in\nthe answer, compare\", the record''s own words behind Show details. It keeps\nthe box open, so the tag is seen. A finding another check also names, or any\nanswer-wide check reporting, still draws in full.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"67b0a73b540a4af290292bf0a74fbbb69d01a037","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/67b0a73b540a4af290292bf0a74fbbb69d01a037"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/984a782055ae289f7fc628c7e45d2fadbacd9567","verification":{"payload":"tree 67b0a73