scriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/f5a0123e2c69da2f3088b6ab8c5614620234e498/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:17:16Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:17:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: open a finished answer at its top when it is taller than the chat history (#52)\n\nWhen an answer finished and the reader was following it, the history area scrolled to the bottom of\nthe message. For a message taller than the history area — an answer with an open safety box under it\n— that opened on the end of the box, with the answer''s verdict scrolled out of view above: on the\nrifampicin list question at a 900px-tall window, the response''s top sat 89px above the visible area.\n\nNow a finished message taller than the history area is aligned to its top. Streaming still follows\nthe text to the bottom, a message that fits is unchanged, and a reader who scrolled away is left\nwhere they are.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PYN5xzwdktSVV3LrU5nuPG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0cc69ed30bdba4a16cae1601de96e05e1779a6ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/0cc69ed30bdba4a16cae1601de96e05e1779a6ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/f5a0123e2c69da2f3088b6ab8c5614620234e498","verification":{"payload":"tree 0cc69ed30bdba4a16cae1601de96e05e1779a6ae\nparent 3c27f484a44bab8aa50f120ed6b49ce80dc324a3\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1790849836 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790849836 +0300\n\nfix: open a finished answer at its top when it is taller than the chat history (#52)\n\nWhen an answer finished and the reader was following it, the history area scrolled to the bottom of\nthe message. For a message taller than the history area — an answer with an open safety box under it\n— that opened on the end of the box, with the answer''s verdict scrolled out of view above: on the\nrifampicin list question at a 900px-tall window, the response''s top sat 89px above the visible area.\n\nNow a finished message taller than the history area is aligned to its top. Streaming still follows\nthe text to the bottom, a message that fits is unchanged, and a reader who scrolled away is left\nwhere they are.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PYN5xzwdktSVV3LrU5nuPG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvjMsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzLgQAJgyaHjgYhtkIt1wAJn8ynRx\nsCDPbTbxWmw+my+LsUaY/IvVZ3T5U/BZkxhRl96lj5QvxKQ48f4u4P66o1wfx8xc\nSmGKVO6fv47wunvtGcb/TRKaOGuA7mxb08YlaufIE2QWmsq0mHwRxqCbEXjXZczI\nUTkAKFFIcQH+0nV83CNJC5K2x1FIdCyqSfvCNgQK0GplOPezln42MhAWBr/1eGT8\nx8f5o4rLQ3/HKguaBj+yUgQxMSz9w0sGP/RTZCtgoLLtIpR7WRYZxNclAGOhtG+n\nuCU2E3q2+Dnt6mALhkVidwi6ImPxi4MHYC8ccQMlkuDVhVdEioY2tE5bqcNITvG2\nzNEQAj6f3taSo7AtrWDkeOJEytiqf7WmijEXnJEI+Y1RR6gHMVRTNfxfsV4v4mQ7\ny4mV1lhLVuqh38JJ8HKyOjz9Aofxk2/OwUiN3faTQBJ1vgxLI7cR5CH1API5vixD\nFOm1LqBwKDEe2n6U9zWgIqZJltE1bcmRWVOIPi+hIAxI6M+SkUECWW3Pj6cMq6m4\nFMtMAc2edDJWcKgkKxUiML1IeV6oOSbehpBhVnqZ8G4V1TIXiHMjX20m7oOjnLH3\nXTDkaXSle3WL9tCay2oE7osH7ZJX32uA+2dsiLUvuOYCfvGeD4BOjehz1CSeLoTv\n7Gm1P92OUfZsoBzw/t35\n=Xkwo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T10:17:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{