wa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/3c27f484a44bab8aa50f120ed6b49ce80dc324a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:03:33Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:03:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(readme): document the safety panel''s marks, grouping and folding as they are now (#51)\n\nThe README still described the \"About a current medication\" mark #41 replaced, and said a chip folds\nonly where no other chip shares its key, which #50 changed. It now says what the panel draws:\n- \"Already prescribed: <order>\" on a contraindication about her own prescription (#41);\n- chips not about the drug asked about behind a closed line, its two wordings, and the neutral box\n  where they are all the box holds (#40, #48, #49);\n- unstatedSignificanceQualifiers and unsupportedEndedOrderClaims in the limits table (#46, #47);\n- the shared-key fold rule and a folded pair chip''s lead (#50).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PYN5xzwdktSVV3LrU5nuPG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b7f4a96565ef50713533d42e40d02a037bbffbe7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/b7f4a96565ef50713533d42e40d02a037bbffbe7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/3c27f484a44bab8aa50f120ed6b49ce80dc324a3","verification":{"payload":"tree b7f4a96565ef50713533d42e40d02a037bbffbe7\nparent be42ffb9c5969962dc1b023d098c32d84d2132bf\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1790849013 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790849013 +0300\n\ndocs(readme): document the safety panel''s marks, grouping and folding as they are now (#51)\n\nThe README still described the \"About a current medication\" mark #41 replaced, and said a chip folds\nonly where no other chip shares its key, which #50 changed. It now says what the panel draws:\n- \"Already prescribed: <order>\" on a contraindication about her own prescription (#41);\n- chips not about the drug asked about behind a closed line, its two wordings, and the neutral box\n  where they are all the box holds (#40, #48, #49);\n- unstatedSignificanceQualifiers and unsupportedEndedOrderClaims in the limits table (#46, #47);\n- the shared-key fold rule and a folded pair chip''s lead (#50).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PYN5xzwdktSVV3LrU5nuPG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvi/1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkfAQAKro1wV5xifnf+djRgdRKrD9\njqtxWUzBLorQebEjjOeajO147wV0/d9pDDGtfwutM+bo1i5aGsb30ilrBqdyu+3+\nGBMpOdXUMVOZCZK2GmkThx0eNLAmVQKBte+DxUCCOZczpjZBdrDM1nAiGnV7MmAD\nIeLDHrAMUYuGySaLCQ55mHDEi4iFMDW6ll0Y2Iq+58Sspr8vgwAPgDXIsp+pTOK+\nTKvQkO1scnBD12YzOu/Zh3Yf3ezEl+h+9EFxqhBCCLq9zncgBXteGsxQe2lmjNlc\n0uF//cIBIAIv3wIcnYOGTrGAqRX5fznuhH2KZNrghHoZMs/t/rxTK+m35v07M1gL\nSThL8GG0/QGHfkAbNz1yDfJ5hhw+DAOdjRyX2OH+6bu/7xtxCueUeW8ITIQuP4BK\nQAK3UgjVHydSonp51NwypGd8Rk1jSZXtPyGd/+r0cSExBQgVz49uynk0Ex4kLfSq\npkXLBOftj/DvRtBieCAIy+nEvq3RKPjiVdGE6xlWZK+UjkJ0cmqDM3NWNNALuJV8\nZc8+OJd1dd1kIqddKLZOEWrUD+l77dg1Oza93FfPRAWSGBgMQNtZAFRwm4MKO/Q3\nzobB0gwajy8Sp3o4QXKdMc4Tarmqk6zXrydujbqLoqb8pnB50N8HZyIN/I3ZiBS4\nORr92LunqhK5Msxm4UcD\n=zyh7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T10:03:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/3c27f484a44bab8aa50f120ed6b49ce80dc324a3","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKDNjMjdmNDg0YTQ0YmFiOGFhNTBmMTIwZWQ2YjQ5Y2U4MGRjMzI0YTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/be42ffb9c5969962dc1b023d098c32d84d2132bf","sha":"be42ffb9c5969962dc1b023d098c32d84d2132bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/be42ffb9c5969962dc1b023d098c32d84d2132bf"}],"sha":"3c27f484a44bab8aa50f120ed6b49ce80dc324a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/3c27f484a44bab8aa50f120ed6b49ce80dc324a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/be42ffb9c5969962dc1b023d098c32d84d2132bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:56:59Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:56:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: fold safety chips that share a finding key where the answer cites every one of them (#50)\n\nA chip whose finding key another chip shares never folded, because a citation of a shared key cannot\nsay which chip it states. So the fluconazole answer, citing both fluconazole findings [50] and [51],\nkept the box open with both repeated in full. The rule is now that the answer cites at least as many\ndistinct findings of the key as there are chips carrying it: each record becomes a chip and the chips\npass only adds, so per key cited <= records <= chips, and equality means none is uncited. Each folded\nchip of a shared key is tagged with every marker of the key.\n\nAnd a folded chip naming no partner, a finding relating two drugs the question names, now takes its\ndetail''s lead (\"Fluconazole interacts with Nevirapine, also named in the question\") instead of the\nbare drug, which dropped who it is with.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PYN5xzwdktSVV3LrU5nuPG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d6c090b98799b49f0ab4fac2c5c5fa9b9c6a0b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/8d6c090b98799b49f0ab4fac2c5c5fa9b9c6a0b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/be42ffb9c5969962dc1b023d098c32d84d2132bf","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d6c090b98799b49f0ab4fac2c5c5fa9b9c6a0b3\nparent f4c9184335a8574815aa129734cff405e4291e56\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1790848619 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790848619 +0300\n\nfeat: fold safety chips that share a finding key where the answer cites every one of them (#50)\n\nA chip whose finding key another chip shares never folded, because a citation of a shared key cannot\nsay which chip it states. So the fluconazole answer, citing both fluconazole findings [50] and [51],\nkept the box open with both repeated in full. The rule is now that the answer cites at least as many\ndistinct findings of the key as there are chips carrying it: each record becomes a chip and the chips\npass only adds, so per key cited <= records <= chips, and equality means none is uncited. Each folded\nchip of a shared key is tagged with every marker of the key.\n\nAnd a folded chip naming no partner, a finding relating two drugs the question names, now takes its\ndetail''s lead (\"Fluconazole interacts with Nevirapine, also named in the question\") instead of the\nbare drug, which dropped who it is with.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PYN5xzwdktSVV3LrU5nuPG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvi5rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgnYQAF9UpW6CX/sQw3t3+rH9PpZ8\nMpLldhmkQmMCscDdH4EkKbEtiHPbIKu9RHsd/fzRLFJfZ1KtbK7vkot2L+xDdpyu\nIQb2UMS7FK+vourkp67SzuxlcjbfGi2x7Wr+MWBEhwIuXQd/o9sRIOh1I9NXw/SH\n52zl1IJdqFkRZTmcaqCSOL97RZN5tJaEZaQS4VDhx35w23YfxQa0Ef4Q68nXlgK9\nDFfrdpfVkVDROjdfEqo0KE0gSePaRhVYLOH/JHF2kmjx6BXGfes8ygA1ofIreK5s\nETlN1RMeoFx+udX3y6jQcPtwoiaIPm0M8h9HclX+4tSxJEfRp9ZqXSe6x52ZK3hT\n179asLqmgbA5FPkIHBlG0mehZCE6+E37FtpEWmQ9LenP95Wf2Hdr0OS0RubZU0a/\nJ0UrwEtsJDSprmKj3WhnfWcMcRvV3t4Jr8XSnaj/tOkiiy/1ciMxIIZFbOauxwdL\naB+DDPZoec/FneZ3JVYLI3YH5VQmTAVy3GzlbEsU3pMCQxiZnp0VJ9Ys1HvNNii+\nHUpLcAJnRJ7G9ZACnx6nRZ/an5M15a5BHXgwtMYFWAu3i5tmZDg1JNKMVXIyyXj2\ncZpIT/VDRGAH/L8raQ040O1B1gYSsN9VrHVMs1XOSMGXfmICRSILcQ2WSmzzAzYd\nYD