ug-safety answer (#38) is removed, with its style, its tests, its fixture\nand its six translation keys. conditionRuleCoverage and doseCeilingCoverage stay on the response\ntype and in the stream state; the panel no longer reads them. The safety-check coverage test now\nasserts the note is not drawn, and the README lists both keys as not rendered.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PYN5xzwdktSVV3LrU5nuPG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"074e8f740f0190cb8c4544707be462d365396e2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/074e8f740f0190cb8c4544707be462d365396e2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/3eddbd8dabec02d0e279ab87ac56ff7bd37db5af","verification":{"payload":"tree 074e8f740f0190cb8c4544707be462d365396e2a\nparent b8e8e548ac2b24e7ab22252db8fbc1204e2d74c9\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1790793020 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790793020 +0300\n\nfeat: stop drawing the \"Not checked against this patient''s age or recorded conditions\" note (#43)\n\nThe grey note beside a drug-safety answer (#38) is removed, with its style, its tests, its fixture\nand its six translation keys. conditionRuleCoverage and doseCeilingCoverage stay on the response\ntype and in the stream state; the panel no longer reads them. The safety-check coverage test now\nasserts the note is not drawn, and the README lists both keys as not rendered.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PYN5xzwdktSVV3LrU5nuPG\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvVU8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA90AQALAn/eQzyt10p/m2Zy9aUGN7\nAEXr4joM9QXG2Vfht3ACMOPLs6m8NNoCCmlE4R5xltcltJVVVOrvOOqlf2rPXW6b\nScbWLWISefN0tALCaHJOXPqwhz/Er3iyfv98WnHg/8PgqYZj2t/RZ+cKUcJYvG4f\nhb6nmIV3Cr0l7u2fO7pwL/6DXtV54A5AUaTvWWmTYAiJuhFWXFZkp3zcug7GGJak\nHaggrwubN/58I50Xj2vIXx6eR21DXb