ub.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/d072d7fd76a8ec046c78e8ff285fd1d2071eb37a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:09:02Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:09:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Address the Greptile findings on #34-#38 (#39)\n\n- A null interactionClaimPairs is no measurement, so it no longer lets a chip collapse (#35).\n- A \"source of\" tag names only indexes that are safety findings among the answer''s citations (#36).\n- The not-checked tooltip tells an unloaded dataset apart from one with no such rules (#38).\n- The below-floor test renders the live aspirin answer its pairs belong to (#34).\n- The streaming tests carry every answer-limit key, doseCeilingCoverage included, and fail if one is left out (#38).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JPs4BNNBoiv8mYSDYrykKx\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ed873a5ac9c0d722f10da453e029c667976495fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/ed873a5ac9c0d722f10da453e029c667976495fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/d072d7fd76a8ec046c78e8ff285fd1d2071eb37a","verification":{"payload":"tree ed873a5ac9c0d722f10da453e029c667976495fa\nparent 04640575f134741435923b8ed073706e170b4bf1\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1790788142 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790788142 +0300\n\n(fix) Address the Greptile findings on #34-#38 (#39)\n\n- A null interactionClaimPairs is no measurement, so it no longer lets a chip collapse (#35).\n- A \"source of\" tag names only indexes that are safety findings