/api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/d24205047a58ac8096045b59425c8cfa257d51e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T16:09:29Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T16:09:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#24)\n\nLint config moves to a flat eslint.config.mjs that spreads\n@openmrs/eslint-config 2.0.0, replacing .eslintrc. eslint moves from 8.56\nto ^9.39.0 and the --ext flag goes away, since flat config makes it\nredundant. There was no .eslintignore, so the ignores now name dist and\ncoverage explicitly.\n\nTwo things this repo did differently from the rest of the fleet are kept.\n\nIt got 29 accessibility rules from eslint-config-ts-react-important-stuff,\nwhich is eslintrc-only and cannot be spread into a flat config. Those come\nfrom eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y''s own recommended set instead, which covers all\n29 and adds one more. no-autofocus stays off, because\nts-react-important-stuff turned it off. The core rules that config also\nenabled are listed in the overlay: no-duplicate-imports, no-extra-bind,\nno-implied-eval, no-labels, no-self-compare, no-throw-literal and no-void.\n\nIt also has no prettier script and no lint-staged, so formatting is only\never checked by lint. eslint-plugin-prettier/recommended is applied last to\nkeep prettier/prettier reporting as it did before.\n\nThe overlay additionally re-enables what the shared config leaves off but\nthis repo enforced: ban-ts-comment, no-explicit-any, no-unused-vars,\ntriple-slash-reference, no-extra-boolean-cast, no-prototype-builtins,\nno-unsafe-optional-chaining, no-useless-escape, prefer-const,\nexhaustive-deps as a warning, and the three rules typescript-eslint v8\nsplit ban-types into. Comparing the effective rule sets before and after,\nnothing this repo enforced is lost.\n\nconsistent-type-imports is new here, and it forbids the\ntypeof import(...) form three tests used to type their vitest mocks. Those\nbecome namespace type imports. In the one file that also imports the same\nmodule for values, the two import lines carry disable comments for\nimport/no-duplicates, since a namespace type import cannot be merged into a\nvalue import. Two eslint-disable directives that no longer match anything\nare removed.","tree":{"sha":"57ffc56f58c546053cf89b31065f3414a76f6a6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/57ffc56f58c546053cf89b31065f3414a76f6a6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/d24205047a58ac8096045b59425c8cfa257d51e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 57ffc56f58c546053cf89b31065f3414a76f6a6a\nparent 3003cd20752c82740381823221e42c425dbc5572\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1786464569 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786464569 +0530\n\n(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#24)\n\nLint config moves to a flat eslint.config.mjs that spreads\n@openmrs/eslint-config 2.0.0, replacing .eslintrc. eslint moves from 8.56\nto ^9.39.0 and the --ext flag goes away, since flat config makes it\nredundant. There was no .eslintignore, so the ignores now name dist and\ncoverage explicitly.\n\nTwo things this repo did differently from the rest of the fleet are kept.\n\nIt got 29 accessibility rules from eslint-config-ts-react-important-stuff,\nwhich is eslintrc-only and cannot be spread into a flat config. Those come\nfrom eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y''s own recommended set instead, which covers all\n29 and adds one more. no-autofocus stays off, because\nts-react-important-stuff turned it off. The core rules that config also\nenabled are listed in the overlay: no-duplicate-imports, no-extra-bind,\nno-implied-eval, no-labels, no-self-compare, no-throw-literal and no-void.\n\nIt also has no prettier script and no lint-staged, so formatting is only\never checked by lint. eslint-plugin-prettier/recommended is applied last to\nkeep prettier/prettier reporting as it did before.\n\nThe overlay additionally re-enables what the shared config leaves off but\nthis repo enforced: ban-ts-comment, no-explicit-any, no-unused-vars,\ntriple-slash-reference, no-extra-boolean-cast, no-prototype-builtins,\nno-unsafe-optional-chaining, no-useless-escape, prefer-const,\nexhaustive-deps as a warning, and the three rules typescript-eslint v8\nsplit ban-types into. Comparing the effective rule sets before and after,\nnothing this repo enforced is lost.\n\nconsistent-type-imports is new here, and it forbids the\ntypeof import(...) form three tests used to type their vitest mocks. Those\nbecome namespace type imports. In the one file that also imports the same\nmodule for values, the two import lines carry disable comments for\nimport/no-duplicates, since a namespace type import cannot be merged into a\nvalue import. Two eslint-disable directives that no longer match anything\nare removed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqe0k5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA