ee":{"sha":"d8ce5925794545f27c75ef14cc5cf7cac65e1cf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/d8ce5925794545f27c75ef14cc5cf7cac65e1cf4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/3003cd20752c82740381823221e42c425dbc5572","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/3003cd20752c82740381823221e42c425dbc5572","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKDMwMDNjZDIwNzUyYzgyNzQwMzgxODIzMjIxZTQyYzQyNWRiYzU1NzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/dc2d5f7973b26785f2556f3fcb43377e82131091","sha":"dc2d5f7973b26785f2556f3fcb43377e82131091","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/dc2d5f7973b26785f2556f3fcb43377e82131091"}],"sha":"3003cd20752c82740381823221e42c425dbc5572","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/3003cd20752c82740381823221e42c425dbc5572"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/dc2d5f7973b26785f2556f3fcb43377e82131091/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T01:11:32Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T01:11:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Progressive-reasoning preview: render as provisional, replaced by the committed answer (#20)\n\n* feat: render progressive-reasoning preview as provisional, replaced by the committed answer\n\nHandles the new preliminary SSE event: accumulates the preview reasoning on its own channel and renders it subdued with a ''Preliminary — verifying…'' badge, then clears and replaces it the moment the committed reasoning or answer arrives, so a wrong preview cannot linger. ChatMessage.preliminaryReasoning is optional (transient, streaming-only). Adds parser + hook tests and the i18n key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* polish: theme preliminary-reasoning styles with Carbon gray tokens\n\nReplace raw hex (#8d8d8d/#6f6f6f) with colors.$gray-50/$gray-60 so the preview text adapts to the active Carbon theme (dark/high-contrast), matching the rest of the stylesheet; tighten a scroll-tracking comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ux): frame the preview as progress + strip its citation markers\n\nTwo clinician-facing refinements to the progressive-reasoning preview so it reads as in-progress feedback rather than a competing answer: (1) reframe the label from ''Preliminary — verifying against full record…'' to ''Reviewing the most relevant records…''; (2) strip [N] markers from the preview text — they index the independently-numbered top-K focused chart, not the committed answer''s records, so they''d mislead (the committed reasoning keeps its correct markers). Stripping uses a hook-level stripPreviewCitations mirroring ai-response-panel''s citation regex, without the trailing trim so chunk accumulation preserves inter-chunk spaces. Hook test updated to assert the stripped text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* harden: test split-chunk marker stripping + decouple preview jsdoc from the label\n\n(1) Add a test that a citation marker split across two SSE chunks (''records ['' then ''2] mention BP.'') is still stripped from the preview, verifying the chunk-by-chunk re-strip. (2) The onPreliminary jsdoc quoted the old ''Preliminary — verifying…'' label; describe the behavior generically instead, so it won''t drift when the UI label changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d5f8697d9eeb4c466946bcf7c03ef0f85bd3ad92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/d5f8697d9eeb4c466946bcf7c03ef0f85bd3ad92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/dc2d5f7973b26785f2556f3fcb43377e82131091","verification":{"payload":"tree d5f8697d9eeb4c466946bcf7c03ef0f85bd3ad92\nparent 20cabdaa102e4b5dd9062f1028f9d9c4362962f5\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1781831492 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781831492 +0300\n\nProgressive-reasoning preview: render as provisional, replaced by the committed answer (#20)\n\n* feat: render progressive-reasoning preview as provisional, replaced by the committed answer\n\nHandles the new preliminary SSE event: accumulates the preview reasoning on its own channel and renders it subdued with a ''Preliminary — verifying…'' badge, then clears and replaces it the moment the committed reasoning or answer arrives, so a wrong preview cannot linger. ChatMessage.preliminaryReasoning is optional (transient, streaming-only). Adds parser + hook tests and the i18n key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* polish: theme preliminary-reasoning styles with Carbon gray tokens\n\nReplace raw hex (#8d8d8d/#6f6f6f) with colors.$gray-50/$gray-60 so the preview text adapts to the active Carbon theme (dark/high-contrast), matching the rest of the stylesheet; tighten a scroll-tracking comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ux): frame the preview as progress + strip its citation markers\n\nTwo clinician-facing refinements to the progressive-reasoning preview so it reads as in-progress feedback rather than a competing answer: (1) reframe the label from ''Preliminary — verifying against full record…'' to ''Reviewing the most relevant records…''; (2) strip [N] markers from the preview text — they index the independently-numbered top-K focused chart, not the committed answer''s records, so they''d mislead (the committed reasoning keeps its correct markers). Stripping uses a hook-level stripPreviewCitations mirroring ai-response-panel''s citation regex, without the trailing trim so chunk accumulation preserves inter-chunk spaces. Hook test updated to assert the stripped text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* harden: test split-chunk marker stripping + decouple preview jsdoc from the label\n\n(1) Add a test that a citation marker split across two SSE chunks (''records ['' then ''2] mention BP.'') is still stripped from the preview, verifying the chunk-by-chunk re-strip. (2) The onPreliminary jsdoc quoted the old ''Preliminary — verifying…'' label; describe the behavior generically instead, so it won''t drift when the UI label changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNJdECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoSAQAHOHxX1PgzboiIgKYiqwSfmR\nAGDQMZJAPLH45RreFC61ah+zFlXmipVmwYcbV7mCWnrZEjDQ8p+d7vCfETs7VcNk\nDLwPW0cVWwQtL+lwd6yJapnVJf0CZqngRsk0PQYKxes0P1Y14KWPEK7ZBhtmj5IT\ndN4ebN0mW8tx6ANBYuq0aR5Y7ZbcNJkBvi2I+IJxcU38MMclLsOPQVrW3k7/xxBf\nqSdsXXQs6Q+LUoIyYZw2pdr0frHygnsCVBBMNqR9z3Qxg4VNrr6lyj91BTvk6Nza\nEcCRL/vL6QR/c6+kuBNDBg8CpsAVhsjgJ/PSGtLMPx7tLRZuF9xlEri3//tI+Fez\nREO5OK8VvblHEx2Rp959c9KDX414uUEpLUsssRgqD8dWciSqueNlZSHnCKaVlBIf\nJuFYRnA9prY8gOKYVQVhd6MSgQ35VUGHVRO9wa6Zu8/Atc4gml2NrkQ89AkTnPKC\nnaVpAZlrYMTuaOpO9wMcG38GwzkMUCs3eBeYwjTwzk282DX/bzbwkeQCGZCfZdbl\n3oZoKdWmtfTYbb6MZawgQ7VBkaE/WTieQhoTmBxYcAXl3cXnT5uY58GWX2FsGQ5N\nXOCfdyPC6l14AivxRn44ZSvqQkiDLs9TsNqrFO6cPCXrT1yQvRjnaBLDu+z0uazC\nCvglyffxZg68TZVs5CPS\n=nETu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-19T01:11:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"htt