:"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/fc3e0596b0e3a741334e2df877638a1875ebedfe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T23:05:01Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T23:05:01Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"message":"Localize the session-expired message\n\nThe SSE API layer emitted the session-expired text as a hardcoded English string, and the\npanel rendered it verbatim — untranslated (the translation extractor only scans components, so\nuser-facing text can''t live in the API module). The API now emits a stable code\n(SESSION_EXPIRED_ERROR_CODE); AiResponsePanel maps it to t(''sessionExpired'', ...), which the\nextractor picks up (added to en.json). Other error strings are unchanged (scoped fix).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"241db27d99841ea4563e1a79e3df87337c8583e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/241db27d99841ea4563e1a79e3df87337c8583e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/fc3e0596b0e3a741334e2df877638a1875ebedfe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/fc3e0596b0e3a741334e2df877638a1875ebedfe","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKGZjM2UwNTk2YjBlM2E3NDEzMzRlMmRmODc3NjM4YTE4NzVlYmVkZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/e6ad079ee58429b9bba1633557a2f39980dc9b9d","sha":"e6ad079ee58429b9bba1633557a2f39980dc9b9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/e6ad079ee58429b9bba1633557a2f39980dc9b9d"}],"sha":"fc3e0596b0e3a741334e2df877638a1875ebedfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/fc3e0596b0e3a741334e2df877638a1875ebedfe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/e6ad079ee58429b9bba1633557a2f39980dc9b9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T22:58:11Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T22:58:11Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"message":"Extract the session-expired message to a shared constant\n\nPure refactor: the expiry message was duplicated verbatim in the opaque-redirect branch and\nthe bare-auth-response branch; share one SESSION_EXPIRED_MESSAGE so the wording can''t drift.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e7bf56691b70c48b9a9d19c79520947c0b8f5a97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/e7bf56691b70c48b9a9d19c79520947c0b8f5a97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/e6ad079ee58429b9bba1633557a2f39980dc9b9d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/e6ad079ee58429b9bba1633557a2f39980dc9b9d","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKGU2YWQwNzllZTU4NDI5YjliYmExNjMzNTU3YTJmMzk5ODBkYzliOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/04d517c74d2ea44553c5582ffac4a0bbb3cdf3df","sha":"04d517c74d2ea44553c5582ffac4a0bbb3cdf3df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/04d517c74d2ea44553c5582ffac4a0bbb3cdf3df"}],"sha":"e6ad079ee58429b9bba1633557a2f39980dc9b9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/e6ad079ee58429b9bba1633557a2f39980dc9b9d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/04d517c74d2ea44553c5582ffac4a0bbb3cdf3df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T22:57:08Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T22:57:08Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"message":"Test: a JSON-bodied 500 surfaces verbatim, not masked as session expiry\n\nGuards the bodyError-first ordering in the SSE error handler — a genuine controller 500\n(JSON {\"error\"}) must show its own message; only a bare/no-body 500 is the\ncommitted-redirect expiry case. Locks against a future reorder that would mislabel real\nserver errors as \"session expired\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cccfd8fc0ab05d6e0c341bc66ff813829c99e82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/9cccfd8fc0ab05d6e0c341bc66ff813829c99e82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/04d517c74d2ea44553c5582ffac4a0bbb3cdf3df","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/04d517c74d2ea44553c5582ffac4a0bbb3cdf3df","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKDA0ZDUxN2M3NGQyZWE0NDU1M2M1NTgyZmZhYzRhMGJiYjNjZGYzZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/5759116ab32fa4b4432b4b1f4f55d92e2fb80e47","sha":"5759116ab32fa4b4432b4b1f4f55d92e2fb80e47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/5759116ab32fa4b4432b4b1f4f55d92e2fb80e47"}],"sha":"04d517c74d2ea44553c5582ffac4a0bbb3cdf3df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/04d517c74d2ea44553c5582ffac4a0bbb3cdf3df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/5759116ab32fa4b4432b4b1f4f55d92e2fb80e47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T22:54:22Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T22:54:22Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"message":"Show session-expiry (not \"Server error: 500\") for bare auth responses on the SSE stream\n\nOn an expired session the streaming endpoint returns a bare HTML 500: OpenMRS tries to\nredirect the request to login, but the SSE response is already committed (the endpoint\nsets text/event-stream and flushes), so sendRedirect() throws\n\"Cannot call sendRedirect() after the response has been committed\" -> container 500 with\nno JSON body. The frontend rendered that as a cryptic \"Server error: 500\".\n\nThe controller always serializes its own errors as JSON, so a non-JSON error response on\nthis endpoint is the OpenMRS auth/session layer (a 401/403, or this committed-redirect\n500). Map those to the same \"session has expired, log in again\" message already used for\nthe 302 opaqueredirect. JSON-bodied errors still surface verbatim; other bare statuses\nstill report a generic server error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c47f7c4ada2f82c1d2c05e38c90cfbe8242c05b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/4c47f7c4ada2f82c1d2c05e38c90cfbe8242c05b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/5759116ab32fa4b4432b4b1f4f55d92e2fb80e47","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/5759116ab32fa4b4432b4b1f4f55d92e2fb80e47","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKDU3NTkxMTZhYjMyZmE0YjQ0MzJiNGIxZjRmNTVkOTJlMmZiODBlNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/2a4f15a167ece6900e23d0cc88744d0ce0dd6e4a","sha":"2a4f15a167ece6900e23d0cc88744d0ce0dd6e4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/2a4f15a167ece6900e23d0cc88744d0ce0dd6e4a"}],"sha":"5759116ab32fa4b4432b4b1f4f55d92e2fb80e47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/5759116ab32fa4b4432b4b1f4f55d92e2fb80e47"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/2a4f15a167ece6900e23d0cc88744d0ce0dd6e4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-15T13:06:47Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-15T13:06:47Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"message":"Scroll the chat history as live reasoning streams so it isn''t clipped\n\nThe auto-scroll effect depended only on the answer text and loading flag,\nso while the model''s \"Thinking...\" reasoning streamed (before any answer\nexists) the history never followed it. The growing scratchpad ran past the\nviewport and was clipped out of sight behind the disclaimer. Track the tail\nmessage''s reasoning in the scroll effect so the history follows it, mirroring\nhow it already follows answer tokens.\n\nAlso clear `reasoning` in stopCurrent''s partial-answer branch, mirroring\n`done`, so a stopped message keeps no leftover reasoning scratchpad.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a1899bacbcd92490da61979583d4ffb7996617f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/a1899bacbcd92490da61979583d4ffb7996617f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/2a4f15a167ece6900e23d0cc88744d0ce0dd6e4a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/2a4f15a167ece6900e23d0cc88744d0ce0dd6e4a","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKDJhNGYxNWExNjdlY2U2OTAwZTIzZDBjYzg4NzQ0ZDBjZTBkZDZlNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/c038e732129fc25c847d794a4ed1b2eb33b19192","sha":"c038e732129fc25c847d794a4ed1b2eb33b19192","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/c038e732129fc25c847d794a4ed1b2eb33b19192"}],"sha":"2a4f15a167ece6900e23d0cc88744d0ce0dd6e4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/2a4f15a167ece6900e23d0cc88744d0ce0dd6e4a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/c038e732129fc25c847d794a4ed1b2eb33b19192/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T09:54:22Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T09:54:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Render drug-safety warnings and drug-reference citations in the chart-search panel (#17)\n\n* Render drug-safety warnings and drug-reference citations in the chart-search panel\n\nFrontend counterpart to the backend drug-reference feature: surfaces the\nnon-blocking safetyWarnings the server now emits, and renders injected\ndrug_reference citations distinctly.\n\n- AiSafetyWarning type + optional safetyWarnings on AiSearchResponse; threaded\n  through ChatMessage and the response panel. Carried generically through the\n  streaming `done` event (the parser already deserializes the whole payload as\n  AiSearchResponse, so no parser change) and defaulted to [] when the optional\n  feature is off server-side.\n- Safety warnings render as colour-coded Carbon Tags below the answer (overdose\n  and contraindication red, interaction magenta, unknown types fall back to a\n  neutral tag so a warning is never dropped), in a role=\"alert\" section shown\n  only when warnings exist.\n- drug_reference citations render as non-navigating, visually distinct inline\n  chips (reference data has no patient chart tab; a detail side panel is a\n  follow-up) and a purple \"Reference\" badge in the references list.\n\nTests: 3 new real-render tests — a drug-reference citation is a non-link chip\nwith a \"Drug reference\" label and \"Reference\" badge; safety warnings render as\nchips; no section renders when the list is empty. tsc, eslint, and vitest (132)\nall green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Harden chart-search panel rendering: citation key, safety-section a11y, reference-badge type\n\nA focused hardening review of the drug-reference / safety-warning rendering\nsurfaced three issues, all in the rendering this slice added or modified:\n\n- Duplicate citation index ([n, n]) collided React keys: the inline-citation\n  key was cit-<match>-<index>, so a repeated index produced two identical keys\n  — a React duplicate-key warning and a risk of a dropped/duplicated citation on\n  the streaming re-render. The key now includes the position in the group\n  (cit-<match>-<pos>-<index>), matching what the safety-warnings map already did.\n\n- The safety-warnings section used role=\"alert\" (assertive) while the panel is\n  nested in the chat history''s role=\"log\" aria-live=\"polite\". The assertive\n  region preempted the answer announcement, so a screen reader heard the safety\n  chips interrupting the answer they annotate. Removed the live role; the polite\n  log announces the section in order.\n\n- The references list built an inline { type: ''purple'', ... } badge object and\n  assigned it where the GroundedTag interface declared ''green'' | ''red'' — a type\n  that a future exhaustive switch on g.type would silently miss the purple case\n  of. Widened GroundedTag to include ''purple'' and extracted a typed\n  referenceTag() helper (also removes the inline-literal duplication).\n\nTests (+4, all fail on the pre-fix code): a mixed [drug_reference, chart-record]\nmulti-index citation (reference non-navigating, record linked); an unknown\nsafety-warning type falls back to the neutral label (never dropped); a\nduplicated index renders without a React key collision; the safety section is\nnot an assertive alert. tsc, eslint, and vitest (136) all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: note safety-warning + drug-reference rendering; correct the response example\n\n- \"What it does\" now mentions the safety-check chips and the non-navigating\n  drug-reference citations the panel renders when the backend feature is on.\n- Correct the API response example to use resourceUuid (the wire field since\n  #16, the README still showed the pre-#16 numeric resourceId) and add the\n  safetyWarnings array.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix safety-warning badge collision: pin the type badge, let the detail wrap\n\nThe post-answer safety chips render a type badge (Carbon Tag) followed by the\ndetail text in a flex row. The detail text had the default min-width:auto and\nwould not yield, so flexbox compressed the badge below its label instead — the\n\"Contraindication\" badge got a 56px box for its 72px label and the detail text\n(\"Naproxen: …\") rendered on top of it. The narrower the panel, the worse it got.\n\nPin the badge with flex-shrink:0 so it keeps its full width, and make the text\nthe flex child that yields (min-width:0) and wraps (overflow-wrap:anywhere) in\nthe remaining width. Switch the row to display:flex + align-items:flex-start so\nit fills the section width and the badge stays top-aligned when the text wraps.\n\nVerified live on the standalone (rebuilt + redeployed): the Contraindication\nbadge box went 56px -> 110px with zero label overflow, the detail wraps cleanly\nwithin the panel, and the 21 component tests still pass. (jsdom has no layout\nengine, so this visual fix is verified by browser measurement, not a unit test.)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Harden chart-search panel: cover the safety-warning paths, dedupe citation key and tooltip\n\nTest coverage for behaviors the slice introduced but left unguarded:\n- a contraindication warning renders with the \"Contraindication\" label (the\n  highest-stakes type; its switch case was untested while the others were);\n- the hook captures safetyWarnings from the response and defaults to [] when\n  absent (the data-flow link the chips depend on, previously untested);\n- ai-chat-content forwards safetyWarnings to the panel (dropping that prop\n  would have silently kept the chips from ever rendering, with no test catching it).\n\nTwo behaviour-preserving refactors:\n- hoist the inline-citation React key, authored verbatim in the link and span\n  branches, into one `citKey`;\n- extract a `drugReferenceTitle(t)` helper shared by the reference chip and the\n  inline citation, so the (non-ASCII) tooltip wording and its i18n key live once.\n\nVerified live on the standalone alongside the backend change: safety chips and\ndrug-reference citations render correctly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aec72b2d095f8e44a514e62c6d0804ebbc45b438","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/aec72b2d095f8e44a514e62c6d0804ebbc45b438"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/c038e732129fc25c847d794a4ed1b2eb33b19192","verification":{"payload":"tree aec72b2d095f8e44a514e62c6d0804ebbc45b438\nparent e2b6cd041ee0eb2f6057a4695eb25a6c69ef1b8f\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1781430862 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781430862 +0300\n\nRender drug-safety warnings and drug-reference citations in the chart-search panel (#17)\n\n* Render drug-safety warnings and drug-reference citations in the chart-search panel\n\nFrontend counterpart to the backend drug-reference feature: surfaces the\nnon-blocking safetyWarnings the server now emits, and renders injected\ndrug_reference citations distinctly.\n\n- AiSafetyWarning type + optional safetyWarnings on AiSearchResponse; threaded\n  through ChatMessage and the response panel. Carried generically through the\n  streaming `done` event (the parser already deserializes the whole payload as\n  AiSearchResponse, so no parser change) and defaulted to [] when the optional\n  feature is off server-side.\n- Safety warnings render as colour-coded Carbon Tags below the answer (overdose\n  and contraindication red, interaction magenta, unknown types fall back to a\n  neutral tag so a warning is never dropped), in a role=\"alert\" section shown\n  only when warnings exist.\n- drug_reference citations render as non-navigating, visually distinct inline\n  chips (reference data has no patient chart tab; a detail side panel is a\n  follow-up) and a purple \"Reference\" badge in the references list.\n\nTests: 3 new real-render tests — a drug-reference citation is a non-link chip\nwith a \"Drug reference\" label and \"Reference\" badge; safety warnings render as\nchips; no section renders when the list is empty. tsc, eslint, and vitest (132)\nall green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Harden chart-search panel rendering: citation key, safety-section a11y, reference-badge type\n\nA focused hardening review of the drug-reference / safety-warning rendering\nsurfaced three issues, all in the rendering this slice added or modified:\n\n- Duplicate citation index ([n, n]) collided React keys: the inline-citation\n  key was cit-<match>-<index>, so a repeated index produced two identical keys\n  — a React duplicate-key warning and a risk of a dropped/duplicated citation on\n  the streaming re-render. The key now includes the position in the group\n  (cit-<match>-<pos>-<index>), matching what the safety-warnings map already did.\n\n- The safety-warnings section used role=\"alert\" (assertive) while the panel is\n  nested in the chat history''s role=\"log\" aria-live=\"polite\". The assertive\n  region preempted the answer announcement, so a screen reader heard the safety\n  chips interrupting the answer they annotate. Removed the live role; the polite\n  log announces the section in order.\n\n- The references list built an inline { type: ''purple'', ... } badge object and\n  assigned it where the GroundedTag interface declared ''green'' | ''red'' — a type\n  that a future exhaustive switch on g.type would silently miss the purple case\n  of. Widened GroundedTag to include ''purple'' and extracted a typed\n  referenceTag() helper (also removes the inline-literal duplication).\n\nTests (+4, all fail on the pre-fix code): a mixed [drug_reference, chart-record]\nmulti-index citation (reference non-navigating, record linked); an unknown\nsafety-warning type falls back to the neutral label (never dropped); a\nduplicated index renders without a React key collision; the safety section is\nnot an assertive alert. tsc, eslint, and vitest (136) all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: note safety-warning + drug-reference rendering; correct the response example\n\n- \"What it does\" now mentions the safety-check chips and the non-navigating\n  drug-reference citations the panel renders when the backend feature is on.\n- Correct the API response example to use resourceUuid (the wire field since\n  #16, the README still showed the pre-#16 numeric resourceId) and add the\n  safetyWarnings array.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix safety-warning badge collision: pin the type badge, let the detail wrap\n\nThe post-answer safety chips render a type badge (Carbon Tag) followed by the\ndetail text in a flex row. The detail text had the default min-width:auto and\nwould not yield, so flexbox compressed the badge below its label instead — the\n\"Contraindication\" badge got a 56px box for its 72px label and the detail text\n(\"Naproxen: …\") rendered on top of it. The narrower the panel, the worse it got.\n\nPin the badge with flex-shrink:0 so it keeps its full width, and make the text\nthe flex child that yields (min-width:0) and wraps (overflow-wrap:anywhere) in\nthe remaining width. Switch the row to display:flex + align-items:flex-start so\nit fills the section width and the badge stays top-aligned when the text wraps.\n\nVerified live on the standalone (rebuilt + redeployed): the Contraindication\nbadge box went 56px -> 110px with zero label overflow, the detail wraps cleanly\nwithin the panel, and the 21 component tests still pass. (jsdom has no layout\nengine, so this visual fix is verified by browser measurement, not a unit test.)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Harden chart-search panel: cover the safety-warning paths, dedupe citation key and tooltip\n\nTest coverage for behaviors the slice introduced but left unguarded:\n- a contraindication warning renders with the \"Contraindication\" label (the\n  highest-stakes type; its switch case was untested while the others were);\n- the hook captures safetyWarnings from the response and defaults to [] when\n  absent (the data-flow link the chips depend on, previously untested);\n- ai-chat-content forwards safetyWarnings to the panel (dropping that prop\n  would have silently kept the chips from ever rendering, with no test catching it).\n\nTwo behaviour-preserving refactors:\n- hoist the inline-citation React key, authored verbatim in the link and span\n  branches, into one `citKey`;\n- extract a `drugReferenceTitle(t)` helper shared by the reference chip and the\n  inline citation, so the (non-ASCII) tooltip wording and its i18n key live once.\n\nVerified live on the standalone alongside the backend change: safety chips and\ndrug-reference citations render correctly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLnpOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPLgQAEC6kEJeDO8agsrlcmKvtXFV\nObhQGtQoUcuYZcgPGAGYm6ixkeotItFLlbDO1yXuQy7CsLSht9IKzYLLXEMxPfbz\nPaRjCL0gjN7SBcuFWKVb+eAdD92KWMiZS9uQGhqSFEdchKVKxLkpBDFddp5nnsnq\nFLGlo5TQSs4GRIWRCbGg2i+HTucScJt+iTyxl+DBaux+WTaVSMVl7XY/jTNbQBgI\n7Ss7ONQAkGiedq5xZiX1S6bijO0A1zYyHFxt7AFflkcEj5yMu+BlxW9WYW0+nQ+M\nV0qVofcStfdwT/CfkICRFphjfdBk+E1NQ68PoYPFvuB90H/mGJE7Gg5otmNrYLmt\nI/lp1IlzjUE/bZKWhzZVY2HXudRHY64vZebpj7Z1Kdq4cVSeybMFBlwL8OKyqWrj\n+a3TPNlVrT6oF8DQe3BJjWQ/XjWhGMzKWgzajPc60CsatQq5y9H8jaZXQTZOvMTm\nxy7uX7Wblh4LlfV3Xbitoox9xTI4yMco+qVMVBZcojGXBUuAEioEBKqQr3JMLuhY\nzLeETbTgh1u1eWWqgS9de9lMHH97ORfpXomXZ1XnAKLoh18591AuhlTkQMI7ZYHi\niQl340DgD/cEzCA7gxtQR7+MJ5isPU/BWdVi/0MOvlVWKFwPAh+1n1Pgb0BpgcTp\nyFL/Ohiy2pEkK9I7I+NH\n=+jfT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-14T09:54:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.co