:"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/e2b6cd041ee0eb2f6057a4695eb25a6c69ef1b8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T11:37:11Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T11:37:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Show the model''s live reasoning under the Thinking spinner (#19)\n\n* Show the model''s live reasoning under the Thinking spinner\n\nThe backend streams \"thinking\" SSE chunks before the answer precisely so\nthe UI can show live progress and the model''s rationale instead of a\ndead spinner - but the panel silently dropped them, leaving users\nstaring at a static \"Thinking...\" for the entire reasoning phase (12 to\n27+ seconds on the CPU-only demo). The reasoning now streams live in a\nsubdued, italic block under the spinner and disappears the moment\nanswer text starts; done clears the scratchpad so it is never persisted\nwith the message. Answer content, citations, and grounding are\nuntouched.\n\nTests red-first: thinking-event parsing in the stream reader, reasoning\naccumulation + clear-on-done in the hook, and component rendering\n(visible while thinking, gone once the answer streams). 137/137 green;\nlint + tsc clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add the new required reasoning field to test fixtures\n\ntsc caught two ChatMessage fixtures (chat-session store, ai-search-panel)\nmissing the new required field; vitest does not typecheck, so the type\ngate is the one that catches additive interface changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f98d0b86387345043b51f6089c8f9cc76c2a88b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/f98d0b86387345043b51f6089c8f9cc76c2a88b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/e2b6cd041ee0eb2f6057a4695eb25a6c69ef1b8f","verification":{"payload":"tree f98d0b86387345043b51f6089c8f9cc76c2a88b8\nparent 4f2fa539e257ba21a0edbd644c2ebcc9824e3d64\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1781264231 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781264231 +0300\n\nShow the model''s live reasoning under the Thinking spinner (#19)\n\n* Show the model''s live reasoning under the Thinking spinner\n\nThe backend streams \"thinking\" SSE chunks before the answer precisely so\nthe UI can show live progress and the model''s rationale instead of a\ndead spinner - but the panel silently dropped them, leaving users\nstaring at a static \"Thinking...\" for the entire reasoning phase (12 to\n27+ seconds on the CPU-only demo). The reasoning now streams live in a\nsubdued, italic block under the spinner and disappears the moment\nanswer text starts; done clears the scratchpad so it is never persisted\nwith the message. Answer content, citations, and grounding are\nuntouched.\n\nTests red-first: thinking-event parsing in the stream reader, reasoning\naccumulation + clear-on-done in the hook, and component rendering\n(visible while thinking, gone once the answer streams). 137/137 green;\nlint + tsc clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add the new required reasoning field to test fixtures\n\ntsc caught two ChatMessage fixtures (chat-session store, ai-search-panel)\nmissing the new required field; vitest does not typecheck, so the type\ngate is the one that catches additive interface changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK+9nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiAUQAEDF/ToxVxUgn4vrGeeco3gu\n+H0w5Hk/Dv2HQNXCgPLagV0YVx2gI27ZebuC5ngesxPduV30qbLqDbrw9GbUpCXF\nAchfr5W95g2CoFyN8wIbKRTfnDUW/n2s+6qYDzW/SzbPRP/KWkNDBbvLU4wUcFcc\n1V66eQT55nOQxDZYEw7CI5E4WspuE4YRSvdbGytqsL6sZL7TsZAHOCUjhNQAsM0h\nW10nQ3nvEqlkJme2SouoGCy8lL7q+U1FCAVWtfI3PAVYeaevtgDUspTQ3YUrjyQV\n2Jd0a2N05e7kM2SirnXQ62F7Wv0YV24bHZXKUik8mmbozvvFn00ROZB5y66yGgNM\nOW7qAHRthLaf5B/0I8YTfGEMeHGoz0p33Tmniz98zRC/DUHBXwIfFkF+hSi7k+q5\nR3ipc8TdbWybWaxAsh5NoGomkUaPp7kJQ2dkGkfEw6Oz5wUdb9d+FKyLsjjDEIRx\nIGoNIy7cH+zDtlkN7GcoCiAlYlfGi6+hfrfh9fzimad5IDPxZK6G2aOUlrrssm5l\nVSMN80oXOUwPLsz4Hu/J3bFcdBru7hIje6zo1C9XT8raJB/ORbvvWRD2eys9vFMu\nnU2ogCGEHGYy28F/W2d/6mDbwQZ81G2P9P9fU3ul14na8XOpvPD6dx/OuCBovpBB\nURUfr6+Pv5snoT7+ZnaA\n=c5em\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-12T11:37:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/e2b6cd041ee0eb2f6057a4695eb25a6c69ef1b8f","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKGUyYjZjZDA0MWVlMGViMmY2MDU3YTQ2OTVlYjI1YTZjNjllZjFiOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/4f2fa539e257ba21a0edbd644c2ebcc9824e3d64","sha":"4f2fa539e257ba21a0edbd644c2ebcc9824e3d64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/4f2fa539e257ba21a0edbd644c2ebcc9824e3d64"}],"sha":"e2b6cd041ee0eb2f6057a4695eb25a6c69ef1b8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/e2b6cd041ee0eb2f6057a4695eb25a6c69ef1b8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/4f2fa539e257ba21a0edbd644c2ebcc9824e3d64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T09:18:05Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T09:18:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Apply trailing grounded-event verdicts to the completed message (async grounding) (#18)\n\nWhen the backend runs with chartsearchai.grounding.async=true, the\nstreaming endpoint emits \"done\" as soon as the answer is complete - its\nreferences carry no grounding verdicts yet - and delivers the verdicts\nafterwards in a trailing \"grounded\" SSE event with the same questionId.\nThe chat completes for the user the moment the answer is readable, and\nthe citation badges upgrade from unverified to verified/unsupported a\nfew seconds later instead of holding the whole response hostage to the\nTier-2 verification tail.\n\n- searchPatientChartStream gains an optional onGrounded callback and a\n  \"grounded\" dispatch branch, best-effort like the early \"references\"\n  event: in classic (sync) mode the event never arrives and done''s\n  references are already final; a malformed payload just leaves the\n  citations rendered as unverified.\n- useChartSearchAi wires onGrounded to update the SAME message''s\n  references after done completed it (keyed by message id, so it lands\n  correctly even if a newer question was already submitted). Deliberately\n  not gated on the mounted flag: the chat store outlives the panel, and\n  verdicts arriving after the user closed it must still land so badges\n  are correct when the panel reopens.\n\nThe stream reader already consumes until server close, so the trailing\nevent needs no reader changes. Tests written red-first: grounded-event\nparsing + done-before-grounded ordering, malformed-grounded tolerance,\nverdict application to the completed message, and correct targeting when\na second question is in flight. 133/133 green; lint + tsc clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cacb70059707004fe323c2690f8eae3ecddec8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/9cacb70059707004fe323c2690f8eae3ecddec8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/4f2fa539e257ba21a0edbd644c2ebcc9824e3d64","verification":{"payload":"tree 9cacb70059707004fe323c2690f8eae3ecddec8d\nparent 38de980799db7bdfcf7dd33d1dbe16d12b898f0a\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1781255885 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781255885 +0300\n\nApply trailing grounded-event verdicts to the completed message (async grounding) (#18)\n\nWhen the backend runs with chartsearchai.grounding.async=true, the\nstreaming endpoint emits \"done\" as soon as the answer is complete - its\nreferences carry no grounding verdicts yet - and delivers the verdicts\nafterwards in a trailing \"grounded\" SSE event with the same questionId.\nThe chat completes for the user the moment the answer is readable, and\nthe citation badges upgrade from unverified to verified/unsupported a\nfew seconds later instead of holding the whole response hostage to the\nTier-2 verification tail.\n\n- searchPatientChartStream gains an optional onGrounded callback and a\n  \"grounded\" dispatch branch, best-effort like the early \"references\"\n  event: in classic (sync) mode the event never arrives and done''s\n  references are already final; a malformed payload just leaves the\n  citations rendered as unverified.\n- useChartSearchAi wires onGrounded to update the SAME message''s\n  references after done completed it (keyed by message id, so it lands\n  correctly even if a newer question was already submitted). Deliberately\n  not gated on the mounted flag: the chat store outlives the panel, and\n  verdicts arriving after the user closed it must still land so badges\n  are correct when the panel reopens.\n\nThe stream reader already consumes until server close, so the trailing\nevent needs no reader changes. Tests written red-first: grounded-event\nparsing + done-before-grounded ordering, malformed-grounded tolerance,\nverdict application to the completed message, and correct targeting when\na second question is in flight. 133/133 green; lint + tsc clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK87NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgM4QABm6nWh4KQAdLwnH6Y3lmDyU\npHf9SxCNFeox8A6YzPfpzZqbP/KDVBkOOqNklo5vANLK6na1aa8h6LGBIX8zgaLR\nuACwZbjoTnk3PD8hM9IzN0E7AtdAeqdY0RjMBoI1yUHUui5nTwhknYjaFjqBjHOI\nOAisAv9vaThwSdlQhOLmPtKRMSDtkJA18PCh1NuYyE0TkZ0IVI+qP3FxFlJn/ALO\nvJs5PeCK4pg1Reg8dORqHfXM7GGhwJDFa303rgDcvxnH1jJlorgBXfSPZaoM3wpt\ns79aJMREhkR4/IyA/M0AV20pUXkFWTFTy2eHcXClgO8j3G/QhVczg7cyVxs/iCYb\nZu6GYtf2P6GD7lxE85p+mz05aEWn0Ckp85NQADRuKW07+gmGlsAx4kpTkeKOwQTQ\nQ6h19eMiKbMU6KI/MT05QVfsXN4moIduoULT8Y4mbU5c4r11NsAK2okRgbJQP8jc\ns540tEWB/kOyeUs4YW3Wje1Nnpeez5i2yaLYeIGMzEQ/8AAd3iWJwacC5YpEla8k\nVM1dUOeksO0jpis5qKZ8hE85CuwzeVM3Zzc5Y/mD46UkQcCFjJE+VP41FfaZGyEw\n+Fn+YpEAXfEl6Jdl0IKa5nnThOW694K764Qd89lhSuipqKfK3RLZ52pUkrCTPTOA\nz+m9bPZ79Cdv1ma64k1G\n=I+mX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-12T09:18:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/4f2fa539e257ba21a0edbd644c2ebcc9824e3d64","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKDRmMmZhNTM5ZTI1N2JhMjFhMGVkYmQ2NDRjMmViY2M5ODI0ZTNkNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/38de980799db7bdfcf7dd33d1dbe16d12b898f0a","sha":"38de980799db7bdfcf7dd33d1dbe16d12b898f0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/38de980799db7bdfcf7dd33d1dbe16d12b898f0a"}],"sha":"4f2fa539e257ba21a0edbd644c2ebcc9824e3d64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/4f2fa539e257ba21a0edbd644c2ebcc9824e3d64"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/38de980799db7bdfcf7dd33d1dbe16d12b898f0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-09T05:41:59Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-09T05:41:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Use the cited record''s resourceUuid (not resourceId) for citation highlighting (#16)\n\n`AiReference` declared `resourceId: number`, but the backend serializes the\nidentifier as `resourceUuid` (string) in both the `references` and `done` SSE\nevents. So `ref.resourceId` was always `undefined`, and citation click-to-highlight\nfell through to the date-text fallback in findElement -- highlighting the wrong row\nwhen two records on a page share a date. (Navigation to the chart page was fine; it\nkeys off resourceType.)\n\nRead the field the backend actually sends: rename `AiReference.resourceId: number`\nto `resourceUuid: string`, thread it through handleReferenceNavigate ->\nhighlightReference -> findElement (now typed string), and update the test fixtures.\nRemoving the `resourceId` field makes any future regression a compile error.\n\nAdds a panel test asserting a citation click calls highlightReference with the\nrecord''s UUID. Full suite 129 green; tsc + eslint clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d142282cbac4b7c96d1ee93a7c985d8b1b04f7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/1d142282cbac4b7c96d1ee93a7c985d8b1b04f7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/38de980799db7bdfcf7dd33d1dbe16d12b898f0a","verification":{"payload":"tree 1d142282cbac4b7c96d1ee93a7c985d8b1b04f7c\nparent 54de651767fc4205f7335f330c86f17e0c9a5ef4\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1780983719 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780983719 +0300\n\nUse the cited record''s resourceUuid (not resourceId) for citation highlighting (#16)\n\n`AiReference` declared `resourceId: number`, but the backend serializes the\nidentifier as `resourceUuid` (string) in both the `references` and `done` SSE\nevents. So `ref.resourceId` was always `undefined`, and citation click-to-highlight\nfell through to the date-text fallback in findElement -- highlighting the wrong row\nwhen two records on a page share a date. (Navigation to the chart page was fine; it\nkeys off resourceType.)\n\nRead the field the backend actually sends: rename `AiReference.resourceId: number`\nto `resourceUuid: string`, thread it through handleReferenceNavigate ->\nhighlightReference -> findElement (now typed string), and update the test fixtures.\nRemoving the `resourceId` field makes any future regression a compile error.\n\nAdds a panel test asserting a citation click calls highlightReference with the\nrecord''s UUID. Full suite 129 green; tsc + eslint clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ6enCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAylcQAJp5kh/ozITC4RXHTwQ1LxSI\nWoef4Qvtj/1g6lpxAjpOWB38ysh3jEzytMDsJZPK32fkODZLxwl4kVCQQCpnmqDZ\nJgkVwMlvQJDgFwKeX20McrBg4Hx0T5XgYiARHpMcqUhYVlrnSpRnfESCLaUMot18\ngY8gy8QA85h8d7ypmaf5fyctsZXVQvbNja4kXsdrQExGt9pCSm1x75YCIgzz8Dwn\nzk4WQ10gQ3UsxYHKWRX5ra7zp/sWydcBZ2fsZs46ZEAVNmWFvSi9BTF6ndOA/Esw\n0i7x/9fwf3B0bDnWNqdrusJCdDS2VMMfEGx6XCHqVMXNpxCi3IfbkXuqJ3/rZIgx\nNH/GWcTmMNdNiJJ4XG8MoHb51j8XkrdqsmFHxGpTGbBok4KiOD+4bbyJY5pBiBOm\nIK8CwQAhZVBtljac2XWMLgYxl2qgyRLtxl7oFG0qM4fTjHg5VSsYgNDifyemtcTP\nsh9Y4C5bkTXniqnNtGf3ZFvE973G39+zkx9BLwEo33VwLhQvIxeqn4wmP0OnQ+Zg\nCz+U54pI+4w+9z5TiE3zPGyzalop5cIdREw6Jjsm3nZNl8mqiehCczNmRmpr1yyZ\nIBfvV6b7wA+VJ6/rleqPU1oxuQ7lnjVVvNDQzKm6SUReFf8spJPxxOVa7Bog+7/+\n/r4on2BZqkAL9mEGm7nI\n=sf8A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-09T05:41:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/38de980799db7bdfcf7dd33d1dbe16d12b898f0a","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKDM4ZGU5ODA3OTlkYjdiZGZjZjdkZDMzZDFkYmUxNmQxMmI4OThmMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/54de651767fc4205f7335f330c86f17e0c9a5ef4","sha":"54de651767fc4205f7335f330c86f17e0c9a5ef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/54de651767fc4205f7335f330c86f17e0c9a5ef4"}],"sha":"38de980799db7bdfcf7dd33d1dbe16d12b898f0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/38de980799db7bdfcf7dd33d1dbe16d12b898f0a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/54de651767fc4205f7335f330c86f17e0c9a5ef4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T22:20:55Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T22:20:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Render citations before grounding completes via the early references SSE event (#14)\n\nThe backend emits a `references` SSE event the moment the answer''s citations are\nknown -- before the slower Tier-2 grounding pass -- then re-sends them with verdicts\nin `done`. The stream reader previously handled only token/done/error, so that early\nevent was dropped and citations appeared only after grounding finished.\n\nWire it through: add an optional onReferences callback plus a `references` branch in\nthe SSE dispatcher (best-effort -- a malformed early payload is ignored since `done`\nis authoritative), and have the hook write the early (unverified) citations onto the\nin-flight message; `done` then overwrites them with the grounded set. Citations now\nrender immediately as unverified and gain Verified/Unsupported badges once grounding\nlands.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"abc77536b018c1b223783861dccf344d4954494d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/abc77536b018c1b223783861dccf344d4954494d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/54de651767fc4205f7335f330c86f17e0c9a5ef4","verification":{"payload":"tree abc77536b018c1b223783861dccf344d4954494d\nparent 973d9fe2b079da388b04a19d530d74809ce5e096\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1780957255 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780957255 +0300\n\nRender citations before grounding completes via the early references SSE event (#14)\n\nThe backend emits a `references` SSE event the moment the answer''s citations are\nknown -- before the slower Tier-2 grounding pass -- then re-sends them with verdicts\nin `done`. The stream reader previously handled only token/done/error, so that early\nevent was dropped and citations appeared only after grounding finished.\n\nWire it through: add an optional onReferences callback plus a `references` branch in\nthe SSE dispatcher (best-effort -- a malformed early payload is ignored since `done`\nis authoritative), and have the hook write the early (unverified) citations onto the\nin-flight message; `done` then overwrites them with the grounded set. Citations now\nrender immediately as unverified and gain Verified/Unsupported badges once grounding\nlands.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ0BHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn+4QAG548tdlSi2nnjUOvLyCV80y\nilTqOoLTq9MRUOQW3BTmFiLINkF9qE/d7ti6g0ewOJbXNS3Uv2xWVllIzY2r6GP6\nvaXT6oFArwBU+JFBfGcozke54ZiliH8jZ8ZhnvyWJc0zOYnAOqKHD72e2S7gusze\nFqnxE993YmkyYjEmodGXQp9KJkbp45NdwjuCwlf+0fg95f05JR95oiPB9uUOe1yJ\nmbGYpx0xWByY/lPuMfd/BUHc2z28vw6YeCbC0nE8+EuVzqg+1dMfMF7qJGPsFBA5\nJAPA33CnSpJ6d/hzjMshbyWyQYQYrmZ6/XN+f/1NRbUVPF5k+QvlSpKKCwi5IzTj\nzm0xd4ogQJM01uI0Y0VzaxoQ9+igETy114mmzoZq3RvJSGHxWMJuqJRBURphLC24\nepwEzALKE80Tal7Zp8lmKIZrh8Zh7Csxf8xhLInq/zVjGSoeViJF5u3XU84wGE6N\nwDY+6CYDFioXmNiPLLDmgxMQfVtPPSXT2w8B6fVI/MpZnDlT6soMvjFf095Rk6JU\nQooyj2agxaUiAFgPWcT22Ynwk7ZGyqmghB5k9E400u+ZV8Jt7SiMlEuJo+5T2fKj\ntAfvt0V9Hfv49tuKIQb9rPFyRgaBdldstVYm4SZfGso8WwOFsuovzKXXgSLSXJJ2\ni5WzkkloXhi7gzvNj+VL\n=ER8x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-08T22:20:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/54de651767fc4205f7335f330c86f17e0c9a5ef4","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKDU0ZGU2NTE3NjdmYzQyMDVmNzMzNWYzMzBjODZmMTdlMGM5YTVlZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/973d9fe2b079da388b04a19d530d74809ce5e096","sha":"973d9fe2b079da388b04a19d530d74809ce5e096","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/973d9fe2b079da388b04a19d530d74809ce5e096"}],"sha":"54de651767fc4205f7335f330c86f17e0c9a5ef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/54de651767fc4205f7335f330c86f17e0c9a5ef4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1390773?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dkayiwa","id":1390773,"login":"dkayiwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTA3NzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkayiwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/973d9fe2b079da388b04a19d530d74809ce5e096/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T11:57:31Z","email":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org","name":"dkayiwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T11:57:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Render citation grounding verdicts in the chart-search panel (#13)\n\n* Render citation grounding verdicts in the chart-search panel\n\nSurface the backend''s per-citation `grounded` field (see openmrs-module-chartsearchai #34):\n\n- References list: a Carbon Tag — green \"Verified\" / red \"Unsupported\".\n- Inline [N] markers: an unsupported citation turns red and gains a ⚠, with a\n  native-title tooltip explaining it may not support the statement.\n- Unverified (grounded null/absent) shows no badge, so with grounding disabled\n  the panel renders exactly as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Render the grounding badge beside the reference link, not inside it\n\nA non-dismissible Carbon Tag renders a <div>; nesting it (and the click) inside\nthe reference <a> made the metadata badge part of the navigation target. Wrap the\nlink and badge in a referenceItem container so the badge is a sibling of the link.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Restore the Yarn Berry lockfile clobbered by a stray classic yarn install\n\nThe repo uses Yarn 4 (packageManager: yarn@4.2.2); a yarn-classic install during conflict\nresolution rewrote yarn.lock into v1 format, breaking CI''s immutable Berry install. The\nmerged package.json is identical to main''s (this branch adds no dependencies), so main''s\nlockfile is the correct one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Use literal i18n keys for the grounding badge so extract-translations keeps them\n\ngroundedDescriptor called t() with variable keys (t(g.textKey, ...)), which the\ni18next-parser cannot statically extract — so the ''Verify translations'' CI step stripped\ngrounded/groundedTitle/notGrounded from en.json and failed. Return the translated badge\nfrom groundedTag(grounded, t) using string-literal t(''grounded'', ...) calls instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add deploy:standalone script to build + swap the ESM into a local standalone\n\nBuilds the ESM and copies the bundle into a standalone''s appdata/frontend so the\nrunning SPA serves local code without a dev server (e.g. to eyeball the grounding\nbadges). Standalone path via arg or OPENMRS_STANDALONE; verifies the served bundle\nand reminds to hard-refresh. No machine-specific paths committed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ad93ce23095515843c021d284d1f2883bd55989","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/7ad93ce23095515843c021d284d1f2883bd55989"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/973d9fe2b079da388b04a19d530d74809ce5e096","verification":{"payload":"tree 7ad93ce23095515843c021d284d1f2883bd55989\nparent e66b4726ebcca4d54b78593855aefcdf7166c90c\nauthor dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org> 1780919851 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780919851 +0300\n\nRender citation grounding verdicts in the chart-search panel (#13)\n\n* Render citation grounding verdicts in the chart-search panel\n\nSurface the backend''s per-citation `grounded` field (see openmrs-module-chartsearchai #34):\n\n- References list: a Carbon Tag — green \"Verified\" / red \"Unsupported\".\n- Inline [N] markers: an unsupported citation turns red and gains a ⚠, with a\n  native-title tooltip explaining it may not support the statement.\n- Unverified (grounded null/absent) shows no badge, so with grounding disabled\n  the panel renders exactly as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Render the grounding badge beside the reference link, not inside it\n\nA non-dismissible Carbon Tag renders a <div>; nesting it (and the click) inside\nthe reference <a> made the metadata badge part of the navigation target. Wrap the\nlink and badge in a referenceItem container so the badge is a sibling of the link.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Restore the Yarn Berry lockfile clobbered by a stray classic yarn install\n\nThe repo uses Yarn 4 (packageManager: yarn@4.2.2); a yarn-classic install during conflict\nresolution rewrote yarn.lock into v1 format, breaking CI''s immutable Berry install. The\nmerged package.json is identical to main''s (this branch adds no dependencies), so main''s\nlockfile is the correct one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Use literal i18n keys for the grounding badge so extract-translations keeps them\n\ngroundedDescriptor called t() with variable keys (t(g.textKey, ...)), which the\ni18next-parser cannot statically extract — so the ''Verify translations'' CI step stripped\ngrounded/groundedTitle/notGrounded from en.json and failed. Return the translated badge\nfrom groundedTag(grounded, t) using string-literal t(''grounded'', ...) calls instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add deploy:standalone script to build + swap the ESM into a local standalone\n\nBuilds the ESM and copies the bundle into a standalone''s appdata/frontend so the\nrunning SPA serves local code without a dev server (e.g. to eyeball the grounding\nbadges). Standalone path via arg or OPENMRS_STANDALONE; verifies the served bundle\nand reminds to hard-refresh. No machine-specific paths committed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJq4rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7wYQAJvVw4CRc9xeqKHza8x6G68i\nMrdkVOJyTsqIMHqFnnXGaa7dp2v+laqAxIsesvUealsLPkcXnMSjoG4pTz8t/yRR\nv1WFm5tL5/sxBGn8CtS9W8VyKz3tSuBI6OxJCPRyaB9uITb1fwut87WoSc76kh8s\nkPdYRlvEH9iUIUy1TjYR6Gi+HldMoUCcZlRYuPwVMZI9X9I43VE0fOHYmZttkIRx\nJN1H7kIk5by1l2KRjfAHHBUoAuoeg+cun/pS13aEbqH5UlyyAIsr2oOabVTVugpJ\np0bXp6oAHceaHeWitV2ot5Baf/ddl9khLDP1/QtiUKVBjrXTTc54Ex7oURoBEmfc\nVNybA08MK51I5ZsI+zRW3ML9529s0im1SGGK7b6BtX/YCeRYl+7VnxbyzLdBqB+e\n4Wc9q2yuVE1Hp6aMLHcMpWcSihTHjinxPUKBvLB3SnID0wwhSugFV9nGUfO3KvQs\n0SLvfF05ljBOu4t1H/ajgRa2niNBv0xdghwyAK8yeO9p8GV4wmMx/X/uDaC8eUDI\nseVL771pmbwcddfS9dll5IbTpuhgbYOoMdYPZaYrHLp1BcogxPLIgMBFKtwmtNHB\nEKaoPGv3cNemQy46nez4Q0kbq1cYjiHbNjhpFhVjSR8Ox5PukbRdA7y6owhRud4O\nnWt8U4ZW7aGm+X4QfZO1\n=qlQZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-08T11:57:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/973d9fe2b079da388b04a19d530d74809ce5e096","node_id":"C_kwDORtovsNoAKDk3M2Q5ZmUyYjA3OWRhMzg4YjA0YTE5ZDUzMGQ3NDgwOWNlNWUwOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commit/e66b4726ebcca4d54b78593855aefcdf7166c90c","sha":"e66b4726ebcca4d54b78593855aefcdf7166c90c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/e66b4726ebcca4d54b78593855aefcdf7166c90c"}],"sha":"973d9fe2b079da388b04a19d530d74809ce5e096","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/973d9fe2b079da388b04a19d530d74809ce5e096"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/commits/e66b4726ebcca4d54b78593855aefcdf7166c90c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T13:11:55Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T13:11:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#8)\n\n* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\n\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest, aligning chartsearchai with\nthe patterns adopted by openmrs-esm-core, openmrs-esm-billing-app, and\nthe other in-flight migrations.\n\n- Replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-environment-jsdom, and @types/jest with\n  vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and cross-env.\n- Bump @testing-library/dom (10.0 to 10.4) to the version that pairs\n  with @testing-library/jest-dom 6.x''s /vitest subpath.\n- Add vitest.config.ts. Keeps the original jsdom environment, aliases\n  .scss/.css imports to identity-obj-proxy (the regex anchors ^.*...$\n  so the entire path is replaced, not just the extension), aliases\n  @openmrs/esm-framework to its mock and react-i18next to the local\n  __mocks__ file, stubs workbox-window (pulled in transitively via\n  esm-react-utils), inlines @openmrs/* deps so Vite processes them,\n  and caps fakeTimers.toFake to exclude queueMicrotask (otherwise\n  breaks React''s scheduler).\n- Add tools/setup-tests.ts to load @testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\n  and register afterEach(cleanup).\n- Add src/vitest.d.ts so tsc picks up the jest-dom matcher type\n  extension. Placed under src/ because tsconfig only includes src/.\n- Rewrite __mocks__/react-i18next.js to spread the real package\n  instead of using jest.createMockFromModule, which does not exist\n  in vitest. The mock keeps the local useTranslation override.\n- Convert the ten test files to the vitest API: explicit imports for\n  describe/expect/it/vi (plus the hooks each file uses), jest.*\n  swapped for vi.*, jest.Mock and jest.SpyInstance type aliases\n  replaced with Mock and MockInstance from vitest. The two\n  jest.mock(name, () => { const actual = jest.requireActual(name); ... })\n  factories rewritten as async vi.mock(name, async (importOriginal) =>\n  { const actual = await importOriginal<...>(); ... }).\n- In useSpeechRecognition.test.ts replace require(''./useSpeechRecognition'')\n  with top-level await import; vitest runs ESM and does not provide\n  require for source modules.\n- In ai-search-button.test.tsx wrap the inline component returned\n  from vi.mock in { default: ... }; vitest requires the factory to\n  return a module object, where jest auto-wrapped the function.\n- Delete jest.config.js.\n\nAll 114 tests pass; lint and typescript checks are green.\n\n* (chore) Drop unnecessary workbox-window stub\n\nThe jest-dom-on-vitest pipeline pulls in workbox-window transitively\nthrough esm-react-utils, but jsdom resolves the package cleanly so\nthe explicit empty-module stub and alias are not needed. Remove the\nstub file, the alias entry, and the corresponding inline list entry.\n\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath for the react-i18next alias\n\nvitest.config.ts used new URL(...).pathname for the react-i18next\nalias replacement. On Windows .pathname yields /C:/... which is not\na valid filesystem path, so Vite''s resolver fails. Add a small\nfileURLToPath helper and route the alias through it, matching the\npattern adopted in openmrs-esm-form-builder.","tree":{"sha":"615f5e33b2b5ac39557482ee3724696927492d55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/trees/615f5e33b2b5ac39557482ee3724696927492d55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-chartsearchai/git/commits/e66b4726ebcca4d54b78593855aefcdf7166c90c","verification":{"payload":"tree 615f5e33b2b5ac39557482ee3724696927492d55\nparent 16d6700d6636ea8489f58e7be2c2367063218a38\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1778677915 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778677915 -0400\n\n(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#8)\n\n* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\n\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest, aligning chartsearchai with\nthe patterns adopted by openmrs-esm-core, openmrs-esm-billing-app, and\nthe other in-flight migrations.\n\n- Replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-environment-jsdom, and @types/jest with\n  vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and cross-env.\n- Bump @testing-library/dom (10.0 to 10.4) to the version that pairs\n  with @testing-library/jest-dom 6.x''s /vitest subpath.\n- Add vitest.config.ts. Keeps the original jsdom environment, aliases\n  .scss/.css imports to identity-obj-proxy (the regex anchors ^.*...$\n  so the entire path is replaced, not just the extension), aliases\n  @openmrs/esm-framework to its mock and react-i18next to the local\n  __mocks__ file, stubs workbox-window (pulled in transitively via\n  esm-react-utils), inlines @openmrs/* deps so Vite processes them,\n  and caps fakeTimers.toFake to exclude queueMicrotask (otherwise\n  breaks React''s scheduler).\n- Add tools/setup-tests.ts to load @testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\n  and register afterEach(cleanup).\n- Add src/vitest.d.ts so tsc picks up the jest-dom matcher type\n  extension. Placed under src/ because tsconfig only includes src/.\n- Rewrite __mocks__/react-i18next.js to spread the real package\n  instead of using jest.createMockFromModule, which does not exist\n  in vitest. The mock keeps the local useTranslation override.\n- Convert the ten test files to the vitest API: explicit imports for\n  describe/expect/it/vi (plus the hooks each file uses), jest.*\n  swapped for vi.*, jest.Mock and jest.SpyInstance type aliases\n  replaced with Mock and MockInstance from vitest. The two\n  jest.mock(name, () => { const actual = jest.requireActual(name); ... })\n  factories rewritten as async vi.mock(name, async (importOriginal) =>\n  { const actual = await importOriginal<...>(); ... }).\n- In useSpeechRecognition.test.ts replace require(''./useSpeechRecognition'')\n  with top-level await import; vitest runs ESM and does not provide\n  require for source modules.\n- In ai-search-button.test.tsx wrap the inline component returned\n  from vi.mock in { default: ... }; vitest requires the factory to\n  return a module object, where jest auto-wrapped the function.\n- Delete jest.config.js.\n\nAll 114 tests pass; lint and typescript checks are green.\n\n* (chore) Drop unnecessary workbox-window stub\n\nThe jest-dom-on-vitest pipeline pulls in workbox-window transitively\nthrough esm-react-utils, but jsdom resolves the package cleanly so\nthe explicit empty-module stub and alias are not needed. Remove the\nstub file, the alias entry, and the corresponding inline list entry.\n\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath for the react-i18next alias\n\nvitest.config.ts used new URL(...).pathname for the react-i18next\nalias replacement. On Windows .pathname yields /C:/... which is not\na valid filesystem path, so Vite''s resolver fails. Add a small\nfileURLToPath helper and route the alias through it, matching the\npattern adopted in openmrs-esm-form-builder.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBHibCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6jUQAJfR7rP1E4P2+5DMMlCjQkl1\n9drhXmgXTdet3ifsLJh/D/FMQZsutkCcdDgBsEqqamEgpYYwachShfuC2TD8x5Z3\nCljcks5+viyAXSG87LZSKtasj9clW+ibbQTxUvyrFdlXuRHAUPu/IHs5p2VpYxrv\nfSvjdbRByYELqd3U2SBTylOAf4l2Pw4/O0mG1d3hlpvm/UDLr/sMSPxajgeI4qZT\nUAiqGiT8mEjYG0BnCbxqXYm4eYZ7hw+ERFKRlPkp9OM0LRi57Xv3T+S2MwmyzfrZ\nT6LY9r6zLB5e1zgpOyTMn9AqFt79NkyDHxemp4y1JSnDf5yI+qCXaYbiK0DwmaZl\nJ+pp0yD9h3ka0soPu27A5YL/NZ4SPXICYIyXa6aEUigTDzpx+Z61+MJ+yFSQW42Q\nKe2/EAge/8iGJhF2corneGz1JwAXt8x0OssXO8HneKO9SriSNRsL9HnlI7pRd3Yr\nyhGxxpjpvpuQFDPhDpLODn5yrL+U6RxD8U8R7PxKx+3dUiV1mIwsirPisFpEtbyc\n9bDuBDIuqOU79Ef+XC3aKQRThvuS16MS4B1/ka8pf6PZt/JXLg8iqLjjt5ML+zGA\ni7ByfNr3aJMsXWR9ytMSBsCR31TSKHfHKnNd/H1iYG9gkZTWVVtpIPWwhNkHu+aj\nwEEerDG+YIxVGCmIvmQY\n=qLSr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-13T13:11:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gist